window.REPORT = {"updated":"2026-11-19","version":"0.1 — first assembly, research still landing","sections":[{"id":"findings-index","tab":"overview","kicker":"Start here","kicker_zh":"從這裡開始","title":"Eight findings, and where to read each one","title_zh":"八個發現，以及各自該讀哪一頁","lede":"The 2026 Best Wiki winners all build a layer like this — each claim in two sentences, with a link straight to the evidence. It works, so this report does it too.","lede_zh":"2026 年所有最佳 Wiki 得主都建了一層像這樣的東西——每個主張兩句話，附上直達證據的連結。它有效，所以這份報告也這麼做。","cards":[{"kicker":"Modelling","kicker_zh":"建模","title":"Closing the model–data loop is the single best predictor of a Top 10","title_zh":"閉合模型與資料的迴圈，是 Top 10 最強的單一預測因子","body":"Teams that both fit a model to their own measured data and validate it against something held back reached a Top 10 at **71%**; teams that did not, at **40%**. All four who closed the loop without a Top 10 won a major special prize anyway. It needs no GPU and no licence.","body_zh":"既以自身量測資料擬合模型、又用保留資料加以驗證的團隊，進入 Top 10 的比例是 **71%**；沒有這麼做的則是 **40%**。閉合了迴圈卻未進 Top 10 的那四支，全都拿下了重要特別獎。這件事不需要 GPU，也不需要授權。","chips":["71% vs 40%"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"High school","kicker_zh":"高中組","title":"At high-school level the gap is evaluation discipline, not tools","title_zh":"在高中層級，差距在評估紀律，不在工具","body":"Eton-College-UK used logistic regression and a PSSM but ran cluster-aware cross-validation, a label-shuffle control and an ablation. Lambert-GA won Best Model for benchmarking the confidence metrics themselves and publishing that its own hit was not top-scoring. GCGS reached the Top 10 with no model page at all.","body_zh":"Eton-College-UK 用的是 logistic regression 與 PSSM，但做了分群感知的交叉驗證、標籤洗牌對照與消融測試。Lambert-GA 拿下最佳模型，是因為他們對信心指標本身做了基準測試，並公開自己成功的設計其實分數不是最高的。GCGS 則在完全沒有 model 頁的情況下進入 Top 10。","chips":["all free tools"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Software","kicker_zh":"軟體","title":"8 of 21 award-winning tools are still usable, and the reason is hosting","title_zh":"21 個得獎工具中有 8 個仍可使用，原因是「有沒有架站」","body":"Every live tool was hosted on wiki-freeze day; every source-only tool's wiki lists localhost as its only address. Not a coding or budget decision — a hosting decision made months early. Two high-school teams out-shipped most of the universities. Stars and forks across every repo checked: zero.","body_zh":"每一個仍在線的工具，在 wiki 凍結當日就已經上線；每一個只有原始碼的工具，wiki 上唯一的位址都是 localhost。這不是寫程式或預算的決定，而是提前好幾個月做的架站決定。兩支高中隊伍交付得比多數大學還好。所有檢查過的 repository，star 與 fork 都是零。","chips":["hosted on freeze day"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Human practices","kicker_zh":"人類實踐","title":"The loops that closed were closed by experts, not by publics","title_zh":"真正閉合的迴圈，是專家閉合的，不是公眾","body":"Of 93 decorated teams, 64 can point at a stakeholder who visibly changed the design. But almost every one of those stakeholders was a credentialled technical expert. The publics, patients and communities the criterion is rhetorically about changed the vocabulary and not the vector, with six or seven exceptions in 93.","body_zh":"在 93 支獲獎隊伍中，有 64 支能指出一位明顯改變了設計的利害關係人。但這些利害關係人幾乎全是具備專業資格的技術專家。這個評審標準修辭上所指向的公眾、病人與社群，改變的是詞彙而不是方向——93 支中只有六、七個例外。","chips":["64 of 93","6–7 exceptions"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Engagement","kicker_zh":"公眾參與","title":"The best education work was designed from data and measured like an experiment","title_zh":"最好的教育工作，是從資料設計、像實驗一樣量測的","body":"UCAS-China made compliance the target after a 461-person questionnaire, not awareness. GU Frankfurt sent nineteen members to a professional science-communication course first. Oxford built a podcast that deliberately pairs stakeholders who disagree. And the sharpest teams publish the lesson that failed.","body_zh":"UCAS-China 在做完 461 人的問卷後，把目標設為服藥遵從性，而不是認知提升。GU Frankfurt 先送 19 位成員去上專業的科學傳播課程。Oxford 做了一個刻意把意見相左者配對的 podcast。而最犀利的團隊，會把失敗的那堂課也公布出來。","chips":["survey-designed","measured"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Commercial","kicker_zh":"商業","title":"The credible commercial sections published a model showing their own product losing","title_zh":"可信的商業章節，都公開了顯示自家產品輸掉的模型","body":"Worldshaper-Shanghai reports a negative NPV for its own enzyme. DTU-Denmark's LCA finds cement co-processing beats its route on almost every indicator, then converts each loss into an engineering target. Stockholm dismantled its venture when the safety board killed open-water release — and won the Safety and Security Award.","body_zh":"Worldshaper-Shanghai 報告自家酵素得出負的 NPV。DTU-Denmark 的 LCA 發現水泥共處理在幾乎每項指標上都勝過他們的路線，接著把每一項落敗轉成工程目標。Stockholm 在安全委員會否決開放水域釋放後拆掉了自己的創業計畫——然後拿下安全與保安獎。","chips":["negative NPV, published"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Wiki craft","kicker_zh":"Wiki 工藝","title":"Best Wiki winners ship an executive layer, not better graphics","title_zh":"最佳 Wiki 得主交付的是一個導讀層，不是更漂亮的圖","body":"Three of the four serve text that is readable before any script runs; the fourth mirrors every page as Markdown. All four build a layer that answers each medal criterion in two or three sentences and deep-links the evidence, failures included. Dark mode, late alt-text sweeps and mascot systems correlate with nothing.","body_zh":"四位得主中有三位提供的文字在任何程式執行前就可閱讀；第四位則把每一頁都鏡像為 Markdown。四位都建了一層用兩三句話回答每項獎牌標準、並直接深連到證據（含失敗）的導讀層。深色模式、最後才補的替代文字、吉祥物系統，則與得獎毫無相關。","chips":["text before JS","/judging page"],"link":"teams"},{"kicker":"Taiwan","kicker_zh":"台灣","title":"Taiwan won well, but only in the high-school tier","title_zh":"台灣贏得不錯，但只贏在高中組","body":"Thirteen competing teams returned six award wins — more than any East Asian territory except China, and more than Hong Kong on fewer teams. But every technical award came from the high-school tier, there were zero nominations in any parts award and zero in Best Software, and Hong Kong tripled Taiwan's Top 10 count.","body_zh":"13 支參賽隊伍拿下 6 座獎項——多於中國以外的任何東亞地區，而且以更少的隊伍數超越香港。但所有技術類獎項都來自高中組，在任何元件獎與最佳軟體上都掛零，而香港的 Top 10 席次是台灣的三倍。","chips":["13 teams · 6 wins"],"link":"teams"}],"method":"Each card summarises an analysis published in full on the tab it links to, where the evidence, the named teams and the limits of the method are set out. Where a finding rests on a number, the analysis says how the number was computed and what it cannot see.","method_zh":"每一張卡片都是某篇完整分析的摘要，點進連結的頁面即可看到證據、具名的團隊，以及該方法的限制。凡是以數字為基礎的發現，分析中都會說明該數字如何計算，以及它看不到什麼。","order":10},{"tab":"overview","kicker":"How to read this","title":"Two questions, thirty teams","title_zh":"兩個問題，三十支團隊","lede":"This report asks the same two questions of every team it looks at.","lede_zh":"本報告對每一支團隊都問同樣的兩個問題。","body":"The first question is computational. Where does a project stop being wet biology and start being a model, a pipeline, a dataset, a piece of software? What did that layer actually decide — did it change an experiment, or was it decoration added after the fact? The teams that win are increasingly the ones where the answer is \"it changed the experiment\".\n\nThe second question is social. Who outside the team touched this project, and what did they change about it? A list of meetings is not integrated human practices. A design that is visibly different because somebody outside the lab said something is.\n\nEverything else here — the trend tabs, the roadmap — exists to answer a third question that only GEMS Research can answer: given what 2026 looked like, what should a growing research institution in Taiwan be building in 2027 and beyond?","body_zh":"第一個問題關於運算。一個專案在哪裡不再只是濕實驗生物學，而開始成為模型、管線、資料集或軟體？這一層究竟決定了什麼——它改變了實驗，還是事後補上的裝飾？越來越多得獎團隊的答案是「它改變了實驗」。\n\n第二個問題關於社會。團隊之外有誰接觸過這個專案，而他們改變了什麼？列一串會議紀錄不是整合式人類實踐；因為實驗室外的某個人說了什麼，而讓設計明顯不同，才是。\n\n其餘的部分——趨勢頁、路線圖——都是為了回答第三個只有 GEMS Research 能回答的問題：看過 2026 年的樣貌之後，一個在台灣成長中的研究機構，在 2027 年以後應該建造什麼？"},{"tab":"roadmap","kicker":"Premise","title":"Why the dry lab is the roadmap","title_zh":"為什麼乾實驗室就是路線圖","lede":"GEMS Research is becoming an institution, not a team. Institutions are defined by what they can still do after the current students graduate.","lede_zh":"GEMS Research 正在從一支團隊成為一個機構。機構的定義，在於現在這批學生畢業之後，它還能做什麼。","body":"A wet lab is bounded by its benches, its reagents budget and the hours its students are physically present. A dry lab is bounded by what its people know and what they have written down. That asymmetry is the whole argument: computational capability compounds across years in a way that pipetting skill does not, because a model, a pipeline or a calibrated measurement protocol survives the student who built it.\n\nThis is also where the field has moved. Protein design, metabolic modelling and measurement standardisation are no longer the specialist corner of a project — in 2026 they are frequently the project. The teams on the 2026 podium did not win because they ran more gels.\n\nSo the roadmap below is deliberately about capability, not about any single 2027 project idea. Pick a phase and start.","body_zh":"濕實驗室受限於實驗檯、試劑預算，以及學生實際在場的時數。乾實驗室則受限於人員所知，以及他們寫下了什麼。這個不對稱就是整個論點：運算能力會跨年度累積，而移液技巧不會——因為一個模型、一條管線或一份校正過的量測流程，會比建造它的那位學生留得更久。\n\n這也是整個領域移動的方向。蛋白質設計、代謝建模與量測標準化不再是專案裡的專家角落；在 2026 年，它們經常就是專案本身。站上 2026 頒獎台的團隊，不是因為多跑了幾道膠。\n\n因此以下的路線圖刻意談能力，而不是任何單一的 2027 專案構想。挑一個階段，開始做。"},{"tab":"roadmap","kicker":"The convergence","title":"Two independent analyses, one answer","title_zh":"兩份獨立分析，同一個答案","lede":"The academic trend review and the industry trend review were run separately, from different sources, with no knowledge of each other. They landed on the same white space.","lede_zh":"學術趨勢分析與產業趨勢分析分開進行、來源不同、彼此互不知情。它們指向了同一塊空白地帶。","body":"From the literature side: light has matured from a laboratory curiosity into a real-time actuator for closed-loop control of fermentation, with reported titre gains around 60% in a 1 L photobioreactor — and optogenetics in **Bacillus subtilis** is a twelve-paper literature in the whole of PubMed.\n\nFrom the industry side, reached by an entirely different route: optogenetics is becoming the control and cleaning layer of bioprocessing, because light lets you retrofit an existing steel fermenter instead of building a new one. That makes it the cheapest route past the capital-expenditure wall that is currently the binding constraint on biomanufacturing.\n\nGEMS Research already stands in that gap. ReLEAF was a CcaS/CcaR optogenetic circuit in *Bacillus subtilis* driving a bioreactor, and it won Best Measurement and Best Hardware at high-school level for exactly the instrumentation this line needs. The competition project is over; the research line it opened is not.\n\nThere is a second, blunter finding underneath this. Taiwan's state-backed biotechnology push is a manufacturing play — contract development and manufacturing, GMP capacity — with no visible synthetic-biology **design** layer, while Singapore and Israel are explicitly funding exactly that layer. A small institution cannot out-build a CDMO. It can occupy the design position that nobody in Taiwan currently holds.","body_zh":"從文獻端看：光已經從實驗室的新奇玩意，成熟為可即時操控發酵的閉迴路致動器，1 公升光生物反應器中回報約 60% 的效價提升——而**枯草桿菌（Bacillus subtilis）**的光遺傳學，在整個 PubMed 中只有十二篇文獻。\n\n從產業端看，循著完全不同的路徑：光正在成為生物製程的控制與清潔層，因為光讓你可以改裝既有的不鏽鋼發酵槽，而不必蓋一座新的。這使它成為繞過資本支出高牆最便宜的路徑——而資本支出正是當前生物製造的關鍵瓶頸。\n\nGEMS Research 已經站在這個缺口上。ReLEAF 本來就是在*枯草桿菌*中以 CcaS/CcaR 光遺傳電路驅動生物反應器，並且正是憑著這條路線所需要的儀器化能力，在高中組拿下最佳量測與最佳硬體。競賽專案結束了，它打開的研究路線沒有。\n\n底下還有第二個更直白的發現。台灣由國家支持的生技推動是製造導向的——委託開發製造、GMP 產能——看不到合成生物學的**設計**層；而新加坡與以色列正明確地投資的，正是這一層。一個小型機構無法在產能上贏過 CDMO，但它可以佔住台灣目前沒有人佔住的設計位置。"},{"id":"dataviz","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"How the best teams made complex data honest, not just pretty","title_zh":"最好的團隊如何讓複雜的資料變得誠實，而不只是好看","lede":"The visualisation work that stood out in 2026 was not the most beautiful. It was the work that made it impossible to misread the data.","lede_zh":"2026 年最突出的視覺化作品不是最漂亮的，而是讓資料「無法被誤讀」的那些。","body":"Almost every 2026 wiki has charts. The ones worth studying share a single instinct: **they build the reader's doubt into the picture**.\n\nThe clearest example is **GEMS-Taiwan**'s provenance colour-coding. Its dose ledger is drawn as one top-to-bottom chain, from 1.67 mL on a 10 cm plate down to US$3,800 of capital per hectare, with a rail running down the left that is green while every row still rests on a measurement and **turns amber at the rice canopy correction** — so a reader sees exactly where measurement stops and modelling begins. Every model input is tabulated with a provenance column. **TU Delft** does the same thing in a different register, labelling every cell of its decision matrix Factual, Inferred, Estimated or Speculative, with a legend stating that the tag records the evidence and not the judgement. **BOKU-Vienna** attaches a parameter-provenance table to its interactive widget. **XJTLU-China** runs an evidence-coverage track underneath its priority profiles, so a high score sitting on thin evidence cannot be mistaken for a finding.\n\nThe second instinct is **a state that refuses to be misread**. **DKU**'s safety panel resolves to four verdicts rather than three — clear, exceeded, borderline, and *not assessed* — precisely so an unmeasured gate can never be read as a passed one; 198 of its 496 constructs carry no immunogenicity measurement, and the interface says so rather than showing a zero. It goes further: because the MHC class I predictor accepts only 5-15 residue peptides and returns zero outside that window, a stored zero is explicitly not presented as evidence of low immunogenicity. **GHCIS** ships the same idea in its colour classifier, with an explicit \"unresolved, and must not be treated as Negative\" state. **UMA Malaga** conveys status by shape and text rather than colour alone.\n\nThe third is **telling the reader how to read it**. BOKU-Vienna puts an explicit \"How to read this graph\" panel beside each one. XJTLU-China numbers eighteen model figures so they read as a single argument rather than a gallery, aligning six normalised feature tracks above a composite score so you can see which feature drove a peak.\n\nThe fourth is **captions that carry the whole experiment**. **Mingdao**'s figures are plain, and that is the point — each names the instrument (a BioTek Synergy H1 plate reader; a FORA G31 glucose meter, range 20-600 mg/dL), the buffer, the temperature, the replicate count and the error measure, links its own raw CSV by filename, and where error bars are too small to see, *the caption says so* and points at the table of values.\n\nThe fifth is **showing the absences**. **DTU-Denmark**'s interactive stakeholder map colour-codes each pin by engagement status so that non-responses stay visible, and the team names the organisations that never replied. **BNDS-China** prints a caveat directly on its influence map stating that appearing on it does not mean an interview took place.\n\nAnd a note on accessibility, because the wiki analysis found that late alt-text compliance sweeps correlate with nothing. **BAID-China** shows what doing it properly looks like instead: every chart on the wiki redrawn in the eight-colour Okabe-Ito colour-blind-safe palette, chosen for luminance separation so the figures survive greyscale, with a published colour-blindness simulation verifying that elements stay distinguishable under red-green, blue-yellow and total colour-blindness. That is a design decision taken at the start, not a checkbox at the end.\n\nInteractivity, finally, earns its place only when it lets the reader change something. **UPF-Barcelona**'s RK4 solver gives every parameter a live slider that takes effect *during* the running simulation. BOKU-Vienna's trade-off widget moves a vitamin flux against growth rate with the team's own measured points overlaid. DTU-Denmark's process-flow diagram zooms from a five-route overview into the enzymatic routes with every parameter printed on the box - acid molarity, temperature, residence time, enzyme loading, number of reuses. An animation that only plays is decoration; a control that changes the answer is an argument.","body_zh":"幾乎每一個 2026 年的 wiki 都有圖表。值得研究的那些共享同一種直覺：**他們把讀者的懷疑畫進圖裡**。\n\n最清楚的例子是 **GEMS-Taiwan** 的來源色標。他們的劑量帳本畫成一條由上而下的單一鏈條，從 10 公分培養皿上的 1.67 毫升，一路到每公頃 3,800 美元的資本支出，左側有一條軌道：只要每一列仍然立基於量測，它就是綠色，而**在水稻冠層修正那一列轉為琥珀色**——讀者因此能一眼看出量測在哪裡結束、模擬從哪裡開始。每一項模型輸入都附有來源欄位。**TU Delft** 用另一種形式做同樣的事：決策矩陣的每一格都標註為 Factual、Inferred、Estimated 或 Speculative，並附圖例說明「這個標籤記錄的是證據，不是判斷」。**BOKU-Vienna** 為互動元件附上參數來源表。**XJTLU-China** 則在優先度曲線下方加一條證據覆蓋軌，讓「高分但證據稀薄」不會被誤讀成發現。\n\n第二種直覺是**一個拒絕被誤讀的狀態**。**DKU** 的安全面板有四種判定而非三種——clear、exceeded、borderline，以及 *not assessed*——正是為了讓「未量測」永遠不會被讀成「通過」；496 個構築中有 198 個沒有免疫原性量測資料，介面就直接這麼說，而不是顯示一個 0。他們還更進一步：由於 MHC class I 預測器只接受 5-15 個胺基酸的胜肽，超出範圍一律回傳 0，因此系統明確聲明「儲存的 0 不代表低免疫原性」。**GHCIS** 在顏色判讀器中實作了同樣的概念，設有明確的「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」狀態。**UMA Malaga** 則以形狀與文字、而非單靠顏色來傳達狀態。\n\n第三種是**告訴讀者該怎麼讀**。BOKU-Vienna 在每張圖旁邊放一個明確的「如何閱讀這張圖」面板。XJTLU-China 把十八張模型圖編號，使它們讀起來像一條完整論證而不是圖庫，並把六條標準化特徵軌對齊疊在綜合分數之上，讓人看得出是哪一項特徵推高了峰值。\n\n第四種是**讓圖說承載整個實驗**。**Mingdao** 的圖很樸素，而這正是重點——每張圖都標明儀器（BioTek Synergy H1 盤式判讀儀；FORA G31 血糖儀，量測範圍 20-600 mg/dL）、緩衝液、溫度、重複次數與誤差量度，並以檔名連結自己的原始 CSV；當誤差棒小到看不見時，*圖說會直接寫出來*，並指向數值表。\n\n第五種是**把「缺席」顯示出來**。**DTU-Denmark** 的互動式利害關係人地圖依接觸狀態為每個圖釘上色，讓未回覆者保持可見，團隊還點名了從未回信的機構。**BNDS-China** 則把警語直接印在影響力地圖上：出現在圖上並不代表訪談真的發生過。\n\n最後談無障礙，因為 wiki 分析發現「最後才補的替代文字」與得獎毫無相關。**BAID-China** 示範了真正做對是什麼樣子：wiki 上每一張圖都以八色 Okabe-Ito 色盲友善色票重繪，選色依據是亮度差異足以在灰階下仍可辨識，並公開了一份色盲模擬圖，驗證元素在紅綠、藍黃與全色盲模擬下仍可區分。那是一開始就做的設計決定，不是最後補打的勾。\n\n最後，互動性只有在「讓讀者能改變某個東西」時才站得住腳。**UPF-Barcelona** 的 RK4 solver 為每個參數配上即時滑桿，而且在模擬*執行中*就會生效。BOKU-Vienna 的權衡元件讓維生素通量對生長速率移動，並疊上團隊自己量到的點。DTU-Denmark 的流程圖可從五條路線的總覽放大到酵素路線，每個方塊上都印著參數——酸莫耳濃度、溫度、停留時間、酵素添加量、重複使用次數。只會播放的動畫是裝飾；能改變答案的控制項才是論證。","cards":[{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Colour the rail where measurement stops","title_zh":"在量測終止之處替軌道換色","body":"GEMS-Taiwan draws its dose ledger as one chain from 1.67 mL on a plate to US$3,800 per hectare, with a rail down the left that is green while each row rests on a measurement and turns amber at the rice canopy correction. Anyone can see where the evidence ends. TU Delft does the same with Factual / Inferred / Estimated / Speculative tags on every cell of its decision matrix.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 把劑量帳本畫成一條鏈：從培養皿上的 1.67 毫升到每公頃 3,800 美元，左側軌道在每列仍立基於量測時保持綠色，到水稻冠層修正那一列轉為琥珀色。任何人都看得出證據在哪裡結束。TU Delft 用另一種方式做同一件事：在決策矩陣的每一格標上 Factual / Inferred / Estimated / Speculative。","chips":["provenance made visible"]},{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Give \"not assessed\" its own state","title_zh":"給「未評估」一個自己的狀態","body":"DKU's safety panel resolves to clear, exceeded, borderline and not assessed — four verdicts, so an unmeasured gate can never read as a passed one. 198 of its 496 constructs have no immunogenicity measurement and the interface says so instead of showing a zero. GHCIS ships the same idea as \"unresolved, and must not be treated as Negative\".","body_zh":"DKU 的安全面板有四種判定：clear、exceeded、borderline、not assessed——四種，因此「未量測」永遠不會被讀成「通過」。496 個構築中有 198 個沒有免疫原性量測，介面就直接說明，而不是顯示 0。GHCIS 以「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」實作了同樣的概念。","chips":["198 of 496 say so"]},{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Put the whole experiment in the caption","title_zh":"把整個實驗寫進圖說","body":"Mingdao's figures are plain and rigorous. Each names the instrument, the buffer, the temperature, the replicate count and the error measure, and links its own raw CSV by filename. Where the error bars are too small to see, the caption says so and points at the table of values. A figure a reader can audit beats a figure a reader can admire.","body_zh":"Mingdao 的圖樸素而嚴謹。每張圖都標明儀器、緩衝液、溫度、重複次數與誤差量度，並以檔名連結自己的原始 CSV。當誤差棒小到看不見，圖說會直接寫明並指向數值表。一張讀者能稽核的圖，勝過一張讀者只能讚嘆的圖。","chips":["instrument · buffer · n · error","raw CSV linked"]},{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Show who did not reply","title_zh":"把沒有回覆的人也畫出來","body":"DTU-Denmark colour-codes every pin on its stakeholder map by engagement status, so non-responses stay visible, and names the organisations that never answered. BNDS-China prints the caveat on its influence map that appearing there does not mean an interview happened. A map with no gaps is a map that has been tidied.","body_zh":"DTU-Denmark 依接觸狀態為利害關係人地圖上的每個圖釘上色，讓未回覆者保持可見，並點名從未回信的機構。BNDS-China 則把警語印在影響力地圖上：出現在圖上不代表訪談真的發生過。一張沒有空缺的地圖，是一張被整理過的地圖。","chips":["non-responses stay visible"]},{"kicker":"Accessibility, done early","kicker_zh":"及早處理的無障礙","title":"BAID-China redrew every chart in a colour-blind-safe palette","title_zh":"BAID-China 用色盲友善色票重繪了每一張圖","body":"The eight-colour Okabe-Ito palette, chosen for luminance separation so the figures survive greyscale, with a published colour-blindness simulation verifying that elements stay distinguishable under red-green, blue-yellow and total colour-blindness. The wiki analysis found late alt-text sweeps correlate with nothing; this is the alternative — a decision taken at the start.","body_zh":"採用八色 Okabe-Ito 色票，選色依據是亮度差異足以讓圖在灰階下仍可辨識，並公開色盲模擬圖驗證元素在紅綠、藍黃與全色盲模擬下仍可區分。wiki 分析發現最後才補的替代文字與得獎毫無相關；這就是替代方案——一個在一開始就做的決定。","chips":["Okabe-Ito","simulation published"]},{"kicker":"For GEMS","kicker_zh":"給 GEMS","title":"Interactivity only counts if the reader can change the answer","title_zh":"互動只有在讀者能改變答案時才算數","body":"UPF-Barcelona gives every parameter a live slider that takes effect during the running simulation. BOKU-Vienna moves vitamin flux against growth rate with the team's own measured points overlaid and a \"How to read this graph\" panel beside it. DTU prints every parameter on the box of a zoomable process diagram. An animation that only plays is decoration.","body_zh":"UPF-Barcelona 為每個參數配上即時滑桿，而且在模擬執行中就會生效。BOKU-Vienna 讓維生素通量對生長速率移動，疊上團隊自己量到的點，旁邊還附「如何閱讀這張圖」面板。DTU 在可縮放流程圖的每個方塊上都印出參數。只會播放的動畫是裝飾。","chips":["sliders during the run","How to read this graph"]}],"method":"Drawn from the dataviz field of every team file in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Interactive behaviour is as the analysts described it after opening the pages; we have not re-tested every widget here. The examples are chosen because they illustrate a transferable device, not because they are the only teams doing good work. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and appears on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告每一份團隊檔案的 dataviz 欄位，皆來自各隊自己的 2026 wiki。互動行為依分析員實際開啟頁面後的描述記錄，我們並未在此重新測試每一個元件。所舉案例是因為它們示範了一個可移植的手法而被選出，並非表示只有這些團隊做得好。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，與其他隊伍適用相同標準。"},{"id":"good-patterns","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What separated real engagement from outreach theatre","title_zh":"真正的參與，和表演式推廣，差別在哪裡","lede":"Across the 2026 field, the teams whose Science for Good work counted did four things the rest did not.","lede_zh":"綜觀 2026 年的參賽團隊，那些「科學向善」真正有份量的隊伍，做了另外四件其他人沒做的事。","body":"**They designed education from data, then measured it like an experiment.** UCAS-China did not start from \"raise awareness\". It ran clinician interviews and a 461-person questionnaire, found that patients stop medication once they feel better and that parents refuse to start it for children out of fear of side effects, and made *compliance* the target instead of awareness. UOregon wrote three separate curricula for three audiences with different prior knowledge and ran them as three DBTL iterations across June, July and October, carrying each round's lessons forward. HFI ran everything through a five-step cycle it named CLEAR, in which **every activity had to report a measured outcome and a change for the next iteration**.\n\nThe sharpest version of this is publishing the results when they are bad. GEMS-Taiwan ran pre- and post-lesson surveys with 140 students across five schools and published per-question accuracy charts including the failures — only 30% of students got DNA base pairing right. That number is worth more to the next teacher than any photograph of a full classroom.\n\n**They trained themselves before training anybody else.** Nineteen GU Frankfurt members took the \"Basics of Science Communication\" workshop run by NaWik, Germany's national institute for science communication, and used its core-message and cloverleaf tools as the basis of everything that followed. Most teams treat communication as something you already know how to do because you can talk.\n\n**They put disagreeing people in the same room.** Oxford's *Buzz In* podcast is the most quietly radical format in the 2026 field: rather than interviewing stakeholders separately and summarising, it deliberately paired people who disagree — a Varroa-resistance academic with a commercial beekeeper on whether to treat at all, then an industry council CEO with amateur beekeepers. Disagreement is the thing most human-practices pages are built to smooth over; Oxford made it the content.\n\nKIT won Inclusivity by turning the same honesty inward. It read the iGEM Diversity and Inclusion Committee's own writing, surveyed five previous iGEM gender-equity projects, and noticed that nearly all of them face **outward** — role models, outreach to girls, awareness — and almost none examine the team itself. So KIT examined the team itself.\n\n**They quantified the need, and built a business model that was not \"sell the product\".** Oxford states the problem in numbers rather than adjectives: Australia's failed Varroa eradication cost A$101 million and destroyed about 30,000 hives; surveyed US commercial operations lost roughly 62% of colonies in 2024–25. DTU-Denmark anchors on a date and a measurement: the Danish wind industry's voluntary landfill ban took effect on 1 January 2026, and a Danish EPA screening detected bisphenol A in every tank leaching test on blade material.\n\nThen the models themselves. HongKong-JSS sells **Certification-as-a-Service** — farmers subscribe annually, the team tests soil on site, passing farms get a \"Heavy Metal-Free\" logo for supermarket packaging that earns a premium, and surprise re-tests throughout the year are affordable precisely because the test is cheap. GEMS-Taiwan deploys through farmer collectives rather than direct sales, because its own fleet analysis shows a reactor owned by a single farm sits idle most of the season. GU Frankfurt chose exclusive licensing over a start-up because an autologous cell therapy's facility and specialist-salary costs cannot be carried by a spin-out, and has a letter of support from Miltenyi Biotec to show for it. XJTLU-China gives catmaOS away, on the argument that accessibility *is* the commercial thesis.\n\nUAlberta's case is the most evidentially careful: demand is tabulated by customer role **with the strength of each piece of evidence named** — two clinician letters of support, a signed letter of intent from one clinic, 86% of 38 surveyed dry eye patients interested, an application at interview stage with Nucleate Canada. And UCAS-China opens its commercial section by stating outright that the case must rest on a defined unmet need rather than on technological novelty, then tabulates the strengths of the existing drugs it would have to displace. A team willing to argue against itself is a team worth believing.","body_zh":"**他們從資料出發設計教育，再像做實驗一樣去量測它。** UCAS-China 的起點不是「提升認知」。他們訪談臨床醫師、做了 461 人的問卷，發現病人一感覺好轉就停藥、家長因為害怕副作用而不願意讓孩子開始用藥，於是把目標從「認知」改成*服藥遵從性*。UOregon 為三種先備知識不同的對象寫了三套獨立課程，並在六月、七月與十月以三次 DBTL 迭代執行，把每一輪的教訓帶進下一輪。HFI 則讓所有活動都跑一個他們命名為 CLEAR 的五步驟循環，其中**每一項活動都必須回報一個量測到的結果，以及下一次要改什麼**。\n\n這件事最鋒利的版本，是在結果難看的時候照樣公布。GEMS-Taiwan 在五所學校對 140 名學生做了課前課後問卷，並公布逐題正確率圖表，包含失敗的部分——DNA 鹼基配對只有 30% 的學生答對。對下一位老師而言，這個數字比任何一張坐滿學生的照片都有價值。\n\n**他們先訓練自己，再去訓練別人。** GU Frankfurt 有 19 位成員上了德國國家科學傳播研究所 NaWik 的「科學傳播基礎」工作坊，並以其核心訊息與四葉草等工具作為後續一切的基礎。多數團隊把傳播當成「反正我會說話就會做」的事。\n\n**他們把意見不合的人放進同一個房間。** Oxford 的 *Buzz In* podcast 是 2026 年最安靜地激進的形式：它不是分別訪談各方再做摘要，而是刻意把意見相左的人配成一對——讓研究 Varroa 抗性的學者與商業養蜂人辯論「到底該不該用藥」，再讓產業公會執行長與業餘養蜂人對談。多數人類實踐頁面的設計目的就是把分歧抹平；Oxford 直接把分歧當成內容。\n\nKIT 則把同樣的誠實轉向內部，因而拿下包容性獎。他們讀了 iGEM 多元與包容委員會自己的文章，檢視了五個過去的 iGEM 性別平等專案，注意到它們幾乎全部朝**外**——榜樣、對女孩的推廣、意識提升——而幾乎沒有一個檢視團隊自身。於是 KIT 檢視了團隊自身。\n\n**他們把需求量化，而且做出來的商業模式不是「把產品賣掉」。** Oxford 用數字而非形容詞陳述問題：澳洲失敗的 Varroa 根除行動花了 1.01 億澳元、摧毀約 3 萬個蜂箱；受調查的美國商業蜂場在 2024–25 年損失了約 62% 的蜂群。DTU-Denmark 則錨定在一個日期與一次量測上：丹麥風電產業的自願掩埋禁令自 2026 年 1 月 1 日生效，而丹麥環保署的篩檢在葉片材料的每一次槽式溶出試驗中都測到雙酚 A。\n\n接著是商業模式本身。HongKong-JSS 賣的是**認證即服務**——農民年度訂閱，團隊到場檢測土壤，通過的農場取得「無重金屬」標章可用於超市包裝並賣出溢價，而全年不定期的突擊複檢之所以負擔得起，正是因為檢測又便宜又快。GEMS-Taiwan 透過農民合作社而非直接銷售來部署，因為他們自己的機隊分析顯示：單一農場自有的反應器一整季大部分時間都閒置。GU Frankfurt 選擇獨家授權而非自行創業，因為自體細胞治療的廠房與專業人力成本不是一間新創扛得起的，而他們手上有 Miltenyi Biotec 的支持信。XJTLU-China 則把 catmaOS 免費釋出，理由是可及性*本身*就是商業論點。\n\nUAlberta 的案例在證據上最為嚴謹：需求依客戶角色列表，而且**每一項證據的強度都被標明**——兩封臨床醫師支持信、一間診所簽署的意向書、38 位乾眼症受訪患者中 86% 有興趣、一件已進入面試階段的 Nucleate Canada 申請。UCAS-China 則在商業章節的開頭直接寫明：這個案子必須建立在明確的未滿足需求上，而不是技術新穎性，接著列表說明它必須取代的既有藥物有哪些優點。一支願意對自己提出反方論證的團隊，才值得相信。","cards":[{"kicker":"The format worth stealing","title":"Oxford's Buzz In: put the disagreement on the record","title_zh":"Oxford 的 Buzz In：把分歧記錄下來","body":"A three-episode podcast that deliberately paired stakeholders who disagree, rather than interviewing them separately and summarising. Episode one put a Varroa-resistance academic opposite a commercial beekeeper on whether to treat at all. Most human-practices pages exist to smooth disagreement away; this one makes it the content, and it is far harder to fake than a list of meetings.","body_zh":"一個三集的 podcast，刻意把意見相左的利害關係人配對，而不是分別訪談後再做摘要。第一集讓研究 Varroa 抗性的學者，與商業養蜂人正面交鋒「到底該不該用藥」。多數人類實踐頁面的存在目的是把分歧抹平；這一個把分歧變成內容，而且它比一份會議清單難假造得多。","chips":["3 episodes","paired opponents"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的形式"},{"kicker":"The habit worth stealing","title":"Publish the question your students got wrong","title_zh":"公布學生答錯的那一題","body":"GEMS-Taiwan surveyed 140 students across five schools before and after each lesson and published per-question accuracy — including DNA base pairing, where only 30% answered correctly. Reporting the failure makes the whole dataset credible and hands the next teacher something actionable. A photograph of a full classroom does neither.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 在五所學校對 140 名學生做課前課後問卷，並公布逐題正確率——包括 DNA 鹼基配對，只有 30% 答對。報告失敗讓整份資料變得可信，也交給下一位老師一個可以採取行動的東西。一張坐滿學生的照片兩者都做不到。","chips":["140 students · 5 schools","30% on base pairing"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的習慣"},{"kicker":"The habit worth stealing","title":"Train the team before training the public","title_zh":"先訓練團隊，再去教公眾","body":"Nineteen GU Frankfurt members took the Basics of Science Communication workshop from NaWik, Germany's national science-communication institute, and built everything afterwards on its core-message and cloverleaf tools. Science communication is a craft with a literature; almost every other team treats it as something you can already do because you can talk.","body_zh":"GU Frankfurt 有 19 位成員上了德國國家科學傳播研究所 NaWik 的「科學傳播基礎」工作坊，並以其核心訊息與四葉草工具為基礎建構後續所有內容。科學傳播是一門有文獻的技藝；幾乎其他所有團隊都把它當成「我會說話所以我就會」。","chips":["19 members trained","NaWik"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的習慣"},{"kicker":"The business model worth stealing","title":"Sell the certificate, not the instrument","title_zh":"賣證書，不要賣儀器","body":"HongKong-JSS does not sell its mercury assay. Farmers subscribe annually, the team tests on site, passing farms get a 'Heavy Metal-Free' logo for supermarket packaging that commands a premium, and surprise re-tests through the year keep the certificate honest — affordable precisely because the test itself is cheap. The cheapness of the science becomes the business model rather than a weakness.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 不賣他們的汞檢測。農民年度訂閱，團隊到場檢測，通過的農場取得可用於超市包裝的「無重金屬」標章並賣出溢價，而全年不定期的突擊複檢維持證書的公信力——之所以負擔得起，正因為檢測本身很便宜。科學的廉價在這裡變成商業模式，而不是弱點。","chips":["Certification-as-a-Service","surprise re-tests"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的商業模式"},{"kicker":"The business model worth stealing","title":"Name the strength of each piece of evidence","title_zh":"標明每一項證據的強度","body":"UAlberta tabulates demand by customer role and says how strong each item is: two clinician letters of support, one signed letter of intent, 86% of 38 surveyed patients interested, one application at interview stage with Nucleate Canada. A letter of intent and a survey response are not the same kind of evidence, and saying so is what makes the table worth reading.","body_zh":"UAlberta 依客戶角色把需求列表，並說明每一項證據有多強：兩封臨床醫師支持信、一封已簽署的意向書、38 位受訪患者中 86% 有興趣、一件進入面試階段的 Nucleate Canada 申請。一封意向書和一份問卷回覆不是同一種證據，而把這件事講清楚，正是這張表值得讀的原因。","chips":["evidence graded by strength"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的商業模式"},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"Argue against yourself in public","title_zh":"公開地為自己提出反方論證","body":"UCAS-China opens its commercial section by saying the case must rest on unmet need rather than technological novelty, then lists what the existing drugs do well. GEMS-Taiwan publishes a 68-year payback against a partner's 4.9-year figure and names the disagreement instead of resolving it. This is the practice that most distinguishes the 2026 podium, and it costs nothing but nerve.","body_zh":"UCAS-China 在商業章節的開頭就說：這個案子必須建立在未滿足需求上，而非技術新穎性，接著列出既有藥物的優點。GEMS-Taiwan 公布了 68 年的回收期，對照合作夥伴算出的 4.9 年，並指名這個歧異而不去解決它。這是 2026 年頒獎台上最顯著的共同做法，而它唯一的代價是膽識。","chips":["no budget required"],"kicker_zh":"給 GEMS"}],"method":"Drawn from the Science for Good fields of the team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Audience numbers and survey sizes are the teams' own figures and are not independently verified. The judgement about what 'counted' is ours; the team files and the wikis behind them are linked so a reader can disagree. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and appears here on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告團隊檔案中的「科學向善」欄位，每一份都來自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。參與人數與問卷樣本數為各隊自報數字，未經獨立查證。關於「什麼才算數」的判斷出自我們；團隊檔案與其背後的 wiki 都附有連結，讀者可以自行判斷是否同意。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，在此與其他隊伍適用相同標準。","kicker_zh":"原創分析"},{"id":"highschool-ceiling","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"The high-school ceiling, measured honestly","title_zh":"誠實地量一次高中組的天花板","lede":"What a high-school dry lab can actually reach in one season — and the finding that the gap is not about tools.","lede_zh":"一個高中乾實驗室在一季之內真正能做到什麼——以及那個發現：差距不在工具。","body":"Read the ten High School Top 10 dry labs side by side and the first surprise is how ordinary the software is. **Eton-College-UK** built its protease substrate predictor out of L2-regularised logistic regression and a BLOSUM62-smoothed position-specific scoring matrix — techniques older than the students using them. **HFI** used NetLogo, which is free and was designed for schools. **GHCIS** used a local install of NUPACK. **HangzhouFourteenAP** used PyMOL and FoldX. **HKSSC** used AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera and HotSpot Wizard. **HongKong-HS** reused another team's tool outright — miRADAR, released by Wageningen's 2024 team — rather than rebuilding it. Almost none of this costs money, and none of it requires a cluster.\n\nOnly **Lambert-GA**, the Grand Prize winner, works at the frontier of the toolchain: BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic. And even there the thing that earned Best Model was not the tools. It was that they **benchmarked the confidence metrics themselves** — ipSAE, ipTM and a 38-metric ensemble, against 5,721 labelled experimental designs — found the ensemble barely beat chance at ROC-AUC 0.541, noticed that their own eventual hit did not have the best score, and published all of that rather than quietly reporting the hit.\n\nThat is the pattern, and it holds across the whole tier. **The differentiator at high-school level is evaluation discipline, not tool sophistication.**\n\nThe evidence is specific. Eton clustered near-duplicate sequences by Hamming distance and split whole clusters across folds, then ran a label-shuffle control and a composition-only ablation — three cheap steps that separate a real classifier from a leaky one. **HongKong-JSS** split runs into calibration and validation *before* fitting anything, subtracted a matched control from the same run and timepoint, and reported RMSE on held-out runs with the failures left in. HKSSC could not measure molar enzyme concentration, so rather than report an invalid *k*cat/*K*m they defined and justified a mass-normalised metric valid only below *K*m, then ran a two-way ANOVA, found unequal variances, and moved to a median-based test. GHCIS specified its colour-classification algorithm down to the equation and the threshold, including an explicit **\"unresolved, and must not be read as Negative\"** state, and shipped it with one-command Docker deployment. HangzhouFourteenAP reported the prediction that lost: FoldX ranked Y166Q first, the bench preferred Q172P, and the wiki revises its own ranking while using BCA normalisation to rule out protein load as the explanation.\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan** belongs on that list and is worth reading closely, because the wiki is unusually candid about its own weaknesses. The strengths are real: a genuinely pre-registered growth-rate forecast, registered on 1 October and scored on run 6, which landed inside its stated interval; an autoencoder that flagged a failing photometer 26.7 hours before it died; and a crop-stress index fitted to 25 years of county rice yields rather than to expert judgement. The weaknesses are stated by the team itself: secreted activity at n=1 and below the limit of quantitation; two induction runs that disagree on the *sign* of the change; a Hill curve assumed to hold at 20 L when every induction ran at a single light intensity; a 2.44× rice canopy correction that is modelled, not measured; an efficacy coefficient of 0.58 explicitly withdrawn; and a payback period of 68 years on the team's own loss figure against a partner's 4.9 years, with the disagreement named rather than resolved. Naming the disagreement instead of picking the flattering number is the practice worth keeping.\n\n**And the control case.** **GCGS** reached the High School Top 10 with no model page and no software page at all — both routes return 404. Its one modelling claim is an undocumented circuit-level simulation with no parameters, equations or tooling named. A team can still place in the top ten of its section with essentially no dry lab. What GCGS could not do is win a modelling, measurement or software prize, and that is the precise shape of the opportunity.","body_zh":"把高中組 Top 10 的十個乾實驗室並排來讀，第一個意外是：他們用的軟體有多麼普通。**Eton-College-UK** 的蛋白酶受質預測器，是用 L2 正規化的 logistic regression 加上以 BLOSUM62 平滑的位置特異性計分矩陣（PSSM）做出來的——這些技術比使用它們的學生還老。**HFI** 用的是 NetLogo，免費，而且本來就是為學校設計的。**GHCIS** 用本機安裝的 NUPACK。**HangzhouFourteenAP** 用 PyMOL 與 FoldX。**HKSSC** 用 AlphaFold、UCSF Chimera 與 HotSpot Wizard。**HongKong-HS** 則直接沿用別隊的工具——Wageningen 2024 年釋出的 miRADAR——而不是重做一個。這些幾乎都不花錢，也都不需要叢集運算。\n\n只有總冠軍 **Lambert-GA** 站在工具鏈的前沿：BindCraft、Boltz-2、Protenix、Mosaic。但即使在那裡，替他們贏得最佳模型的也不是工具，而是他們**對信心指標本身做了基準測試**——拿 ipSAE、ipTM 與一組 38 項指標的集成，去對照 5,721 個有實驗標註的設計——發現該集成的 ROC-AUC 只有 0.541，幾乎只比亂猜好一點，還注意到自己最後成功的那個設計分數並不是最高的，然後把這一切全部公開，而不是安靜地只報成功的那一個。\n\n這就是整個型態，而且在整個層級中都成立。**高中層級的差異來自評估的紀律，而不是工具的精密度。**\n\n證據很具體。Eton 以 Hamming 距離把近似重複的序列分群，再把整群一起分到同一個 fold，接著跑標籤洗牌對照與僅用胺基酸組成的消融測試——三個便宜的步驟，就把一個真正的分類器和一個資料外洩的分類器分開了。**HongKong-JSS** 在擬合任何東西*之前*就把實驗批次分成校正組與驗證組，扣除同一批次、同一時間點的對照，並在保留批次上報告 RMSE，而且把失敗的資料留在裡面。HKSSC 無法量到酵素的莫耳濃度，於是沒有去報一個無效的 *k*cat/*K*m，而是定義並論證了一個只在低於 *K*m 時有效的質量標準化指標，接著做雙因子 ANOVA，發現變異數不齊，再改用以中位數為基礎的檢定。GHCIS 把顏色判讀演算法寫到方程式與閾值的層級，包含一個明確的**「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」**狀態，並以一行指令的 Docker 部署出貨。HangzhouFourteenAP 報告了那個輸掉的預測：FoldX 把 Y166Q 排第一，實驗卻偏好 Q172P，而 wiki 修正了自己的排序，同時用 BCA 標準化排除「蛋白質上樣量不同」這個解釋。\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan** 也屬於這份名單，而且值得仔細讀，因為這個 wiki 對自身弱點的坦白程度相當罕見。強項是真的：一個貨真價實的預先登記成長率預測，10 月 1 日登記、在第 6 批次評分，結果落在所宣告的區間內；一個在光度計故障前 26.7 小時就示警的自編碼器；以及一個以 25 年各縣市稻作產量擬合、而非靠專家判斷加權的作物逆境指數。弱點則由團隊自己寫出來：分泌活性 n=1 且低於定量極限；兩次誘導實驗對變化的*正負號*彼此矛盾；Hill 曲線被假定在 20 公升仍然成立，但所有誘導都只在單一光強度下進行；2.44 倍的水稻冠層修正是模擬出來而非量出來的；一個 0.58 的效能係數被明確撤回；以及以團隊自己的損失數字計算出 68 年的回收期，對比合作夥伴算出的 4.9 年，而這個歧異被指名寫出，而不是被解決掉。把歧異寫出來、而不是挑一個好看的數字，正是值得保留的做法。\n\n**還有對照組。** **GCGS** 在完全沒有 model 頁也沒有 software 頁的情況下進入高中組 Top 10——兩個路徑都回傳 404。它唯一的建模主張，是一個沒有記載參數、方程式或工具名稱的電路層級模擬。一支隊伍確實可以幾乎沒有乾實驗室，仍然進入該組前十名。但 GCGS 做不到的是拿下建模、測量或軟體獎項——而那正是機會的確切形狀。","cards":[{"kicker":"The ceiling","title":"Lambert-GA, and what the frontier costs","title_zh":"Lambert-GA，以及站上前沿的代價","body":"Four linked models: protein-design metric benchmarking on 5,721 labelled designs, a Sobol-analysed oral pharmacokinetic model, a 13-ODE SimBiology RNAi network, and an individual-based six-year, 800-run colony epidemiology. They produced the first reported DWV VP3 minibinder for under $400 of compute, released the open-source PRINCE site ranker (45.8% top-3 hit rate against 23.8% random on a no-homolog subset), and an $80 dryer externally validated at two universities. This is the ceiling, and it is reachable.","body_zh":"四個彼此連動的模型：在 5,721 個有標註的設計上做蛋白質設計指標的基準測試、一個經 Sobol 分析的口服藥物動力學模型、一個 13 條 ODE 的 SimBiology RNAi 網路，以及一個為期六年、跑 800 次的個體導向族群流行病學模擬。他們以不到 400 美元的運算成本做出第一個被報導的 DWV VP3 minibinder，釋出開源的 PRINCE 位點排序工具（在無同源子集上，前三名命中率 45.8%，對照隨機的 23.8%），以及一台 80 美元、經兩所大學外部驗證的乾燥裝置。這就是天花板，而且搆得到。","chips":["Boltz-2 · BindCraft · Protenix","under $400 of compute"],"kicker_zh":"天花板"},{"kicker":"The floor","title":"GCGS: Top 10 with no dry lab at all","title_zh":"GCGS：完全沒有乾實驗室也能進 Top 10","body":"Both /model and /software return 404. The single modelling claim is an undocumented circuit-level simulation with no parameters, equations or tooling named. GCGS still reached the High School Top 10 on the strength of a clean two-cycle DBTL and its Best New Improved Part. Read it as the honest floor: the dry lab is not what gets you into the top ten — it is what gets you a prize.","body_zh":"/model 與 /software 都回傳 404。唯一的建模主張是一個沒有記載參數、方程式或工具名稱的電路層級模擬。GCGS 仍然憑著乾淨的兩輪 DBTL 與最佳改良基因元件獎進入高中組 Top 10。請把它讀成誠實的底線：乾實驗室不是讓你擠進前十名的東西——它是讓你拿到獎項的東西。","chips":["no model page","still Top 10"],"kicker_zh":"地板"},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Three cheap controls that separate real from leaky","title_zh":"三個便宜的對照，分開真實與外洩","body":"From Eton-College-UK, and transferable to any student machine-learning project: cluster near-duplicate sequences by Hamming distance and split whole clusters across folds, so the model cannot memorise a near-copy; run a label-shuffle control, which must collapse to chance; run an ablation that strips the information you claim to be using. None of these needs a GPU. Together they turn a high-school classifier into something a reviewer can believe.","body_zh":"來自 Eton-College-UK，可移植到任何學生的機器學習專案：以 Hamming 距離把近似重複的序列分群，並把整群分到同一個 fold，讓模型無法記住近似副本；跑標籤洗牌對照，其表現必須塌回隨機水準；跑一個消融測試，剝除你宣稱正在使用的那項資訊。這些都不需要 GPU。合起來，它們能把一個高中生的分類器變成審閱者願意相信的東西。","chips":["cluster-aware CV","label shuffle","ablation"],"kicker_zh":"共同型態"},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Split before you fit","title_zh":"先切分，再擬合","body":"HongKong-JSS divided its runs into calibration and validation before fitting anything, subtracted a matched control from the same run and timepoint, inverted the fit to predict unknowns, and reported RMSE on the held-out runs with the failures left in — then published a list of the statistics they had not yet done. That last habit is rarer and more valuable than the first.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 在擬合任何東西之前就把實驗批次分成校正組與驗證組，扣除同一批次、同一時間點的對照，反解擬合式來預測未知樣本，並在保留批次上報告 RMSE、把失敗的資料留在裡面——接著公布了一份他們還沒做的統計分析清單。最後這個習慣比第一個更罕見，也更有價值。","chips":["held-out RMSE","published what is not yet done"],"kicker_zh":"共同型態"},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Publish the prediction that lost","title_zh":"公開那個輸掉的預測","body":"HangzhouFourteenAP's FoldX pipeline ranked Y166Q first; the bench preferred Q172P. Rather than bury it, the wiki revises its own ranking, demotes the failed candidate to a mechanistic probe, and uses BCA normalisation to rule out protein load as the confound. Lambert-GA did the same at a larger scale by showing its own hit was not the top-scoring design. A dry lab earns more credibility from one well-controlled loss than from three unexamined wins.","body_zh":"HangzhouFourteenAP 的 FoldX 流程把 Y166Q 排第一，實驗卻偏好 Q172P。他們沒有把它埋掉，而是在 wiki 上修正自己的排序，把失敗的候選降級為機制探針，並以 BCA 標準化排除「蛋白質上樣量」這個干擾因子。Lambert-GA 在更大的尺度上做了同樣的事：證明自己成功的那個設計並不是分數最高的。一個乾實驗室從一次控制良好的失敗中得到的可信度，大於三次未經檢驗的成功。","chips":["FoldX said Y166Q","the bench said Q172P"],"kicker_zh":"共同型態"},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"The gap is one term of teaching, not a budget line","title_zh":"差距是一個學期的教學，不是一筆預算","body":"Every practice above — cluster-aware splits, label-shuffle controls, calibration/validation separation, provenance tagging, publishing the loss — costs nothing but attention and can be taught in a term. The tools the 2026 high-school field actually used are free: NetLogo, NUPACK, PyMOL, FoldX, scikit-learn, ImageJ, Chimera, the AlphaFold server. GEMS does not need to buy its way to the ceiling. It needs to make evaluation discipline the house style.","body_zh":"上述每一項做法——分群感知的資料切分、標籤洗牌對照、校正與驗證分離、來源標註、公開失敗——都不花錢，只花注意力，而且一個學期就能教完。2026 年高中組實際用到的工具都是免費的：NetLogo、NUPACK、PyMOL、FoldX、scikit-learn、ImageJ、Chimera、AlphaFold server。GEMS 不需要靠花錢爬上天花板，它需要的是把評估紀律變成自己的風格。","chips":["all free tools","one term"],"kicker_zh":"給 GEMS"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Headline dry-lab work","Main tools","The discipline that stands out"],"head_zh":["團隊","乾實驗室重點工作","主要工具","最突出的紀律"],"rows":[["Lambert-GA","Four linked models: de novo minibinder design, oral PK, 13-ODE RNAi network, colony epidemiology","BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic","Benchmarked the confidence metrics themselves and published that its own hit was not top-scoring"],["Eton-College-UK","Seven-protease substrate predictor on 10,472 cleavage windows","scikit-learn, PSSM, BLOSUM62, VHSE","Hamming-cluster-aware cross-validation, label-shuffle and ablation controls"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Crop-stress index fitted to 25 years of county rice yields; optogenetic circuit; anomaly detection","Python, autoencoder, Kalman filter, ERA5, QGIS, AlphaFold","A pre-registered forecast scored after the fact, and a published disagreement between its own runs"],["GHCIS","Toehold design pipeline, plus ARGUS, a deployable colour-classification platform","NUPACK 4.1.0.1, Node.js, Docker, SQLite","Algorithm specified to the threshold, with an explicit 'unresolved' state"],["HongKong-JSS","Calibration and inverse prediction for an in-field mercury assay","ImageJ, log-linear calibration, Onshape, ESP32","Calibration/validation split before fitting; RMSE on held-out runs with failures left in"],["HKSSC","Structure-guided mutagenesis and enzyme kinetics for a paraben-degrading esterase","AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera, HotSpot Wizard, CB-Dock2","Invented a justified mass-normalised metric rather than report an invalid kcat/Km"],["HFI","Agent-based contact model and a 13-variable ODE system, both as wet-lab gatekeepers","NetLogo 3D, Runge-Kutta, interactive HTML front-ends","Screened seven RBS parts computationally before a single plasmid was built"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","Mutation prioritisation pipeline for CoGH66","PyMOL, FoldX, MAFFT, AlphaFold Server","Reported the computational prediction the bench overturned, with the confound controlled"],["HongKong-HS","Toehold switch thermodynamics for a urinary miRNA screening kit","NUPACK, miRADAR (Wageningen iGEM 2024)","Reused another team's released tool instead of rebuilding it"],["GCGS","No model or software page exists","—","The control case: Top 10 without a dry lab, but no modelling prize"]]},"method":"Drawn from the ten High School Top 10 team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Tool lists are what each team names; a team may have used more than it wrote down. The judgement about what 'stands out' is ours, and a reader who disagrees should open the team file and the wiki behind it — both are linked. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and has been assessed on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料來自本報告中高中組 Top 10 的十份團隊檔案，每一份都取自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。工具清單是各隊自己寫出來的；團隊實際用到的可能多於其所記載。關於「什麼最突出」的判斷出自我們，不同意的讀者可以直接打開團隊檔案與其背後的 wiki——兩者都有連結。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，評判標準與其他隊伍相同。","kicker_zh":"原創分析"},{"id":"ihp-depth","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Who actually let the outside world change the science","lede":"Across 93 teams, closing the loop has stopped being the distinction and become the norm — and almost every loop that closed was closed by a credentialled expert rather than by anybody the criterion is rhetorically about.","body":"A score of four is a sentence, not a stakeholder list: a name, a specific thing said, and a design that is visibly different afterwards. Wageningen's Triton has three modules rather than one because Peter Fischer of Aqualab Zuid explained that trifluoroacetate can only be measured by LC-MS at a central lab, which forced an on-site biosensor, and because Bert van der Waal and Peyman Salehian showed that even tenfold reverse-osmosis concentration leaves it far too dilute, which forced a capture module. **GEMS-Taiwan** was releasing engineered Bacillus into soil until Prof. Chen Wen-Liang told them it could be neither contained nor made to sense temperature precisely; the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor and the electronic AIoT sensing layer both came out of that one April conversation. UCAS-China dropped NKX2-1 as a cargo and put SLPI in its place because Professor Huaiyong Chen said the first matters in development and barely in adulthood. RDFZ-China built bcsABCD in both BL21(DE3) and C41(DE3) and switched host after Professor Haibo Zhang warned that a working genetic module does not imply an efficient one; WUXI-DSAS excised gtdT on Dr Tengfei Hu's advice and recovered the linear dose-response its first-generation sensor could not give; IISER-Kolkata rebuilt its kill-switch trigger around the hypochlorite-sensing regulator RclR after a wastewater engineer pointed out that Indian plants disinfect with sodium hypochlorite rather than UV; and Oxford gave up a living Snodgrassella symbiont for heat-inactivated yeast because regulators pushed back against the beekeepers who had asked for it, then published what that cost its own users.\n\nThe three Best IHP winners share a method, and it is organisational rather than intellectual: the practice is wired into the engineering, not appended to it. **TU Delft** ran Value Sensitive Design in three declared passes and translated values into requirements, labelling the ones it could not meet as Future Perspectives rather than dropping them quietly; UCAS-China built its RCSF cycle as a deliberate parallel to DBTL and gave the human practices group the standing job of tracking every subteam's bottleneck; GEMS-Taiwan ran four thematic expert pipelines with five continuously engaged experts. What the winners do not have is a monopoly on depth. Oxford, Wageningen and UFABC-Brazil were nominees with chains at least as traceable, and UFABC declared its confirmation and refutation rules before seeing its survey results, then redrew its own SWOT when two assumptions failed. **Madrid-UCM**, which published the only genuine closure criterion in the cohort, got no human practices nomination at all.\n\nThe formats that changed designs are narrow and unglamorous. One of them is a single conversation with whoever operates the thing: Veolia's technical director for LYON, a sulfur-recovery engineer of thirty-three years for UOttawa, an optometrist for UAlberta, wet-market vendors for HongKong-JSS who demanded a number and got a wavelength-resolved spectrometer in place of a 14-channel colour sensor. Another is protocol-level consultation with whoever actually runs the technique, which is where chassis and construct changes come from: DTU to Komagataella phaffii, NFLSHS-CHINA from two plasmids to one, Heidelberg to a Serratia expression cassette. Add regulators contacted while the design is still open, peer teams handing over negative data as Darmstadt 2025 did to Padua on pcrABCD's oxygen sensitivity, and written-scorecard pitch events, which are cheap and work: Stanford's BIOME Shark Tank produced the microneedle segmentation pipeline. Against that, the school workshop, the museum stand, the carnival booth, the panel discussion and SDG mapping produced headcounts and nothing traceable, and the large public survey changed vocabulary with near-perfect reliability and hardware almost never.\n\nThe high-school tier is fully competitive wherever the work is user-facing and iterative. HongKong-JSS's farm-driven hardware revisions, measured as a drop from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent coefficient of variation, are better user-led engineering than most collegiate teams managed; **Hongwen School** struck three marketing claims on a gastroenterologist's evidence ladder and changed its selection antibiotic on a professor's re-annotation; HFI, NFLSHS-CHINA, RDFZ-China and WUXI-DSAS all changed circuits or hosts for a named reason; and QingdaoAcademy compressed twenty-two activities into thirteen numbered decisions that split a one-pot process in two and abandoned a planned pH-based function switch outright. Where the tier is not competitive is institutional reach: nothing in it approaches Oxford's EPA-FDA-USDA-CBD mapping, Wageningen's analysis of the non-viable-GMO approval route, UCL's Water UK discharge gap or DTU's correspondence with the European Environment Agency, and formal ethics infrastructure is rare, with Baltimore's community-lab board the main exception; the tier also almost never publishes failures of access the way DTU names the turbine makers who never replied.\n\nThe uncomfortable finding is who actually caused the changes. Of 64 teams that closed a loop, the loop was closed by a credentialled technical expert in nearly every case; the publics, patients and communities that the criterion is rhetorically about overwhelmingly changed the vocabulary and not the vector. Cornell's burn survivors changed what the team promises, Princeton's myeloma patients changed the word 'virus', HFI's 434 respondents changed 'genetically modified' to 'engineered' — all real, none of it touching a construct. Genuine counter-examples number six or seven in 93: LYON removed every living cell from its filter because the public objected, ICJFLS turned public fear into a four-layer containment design, HongKong-JSS re-specified a sensor because farmers wanted a number, UFABC-Brazil routed its seizure alert to a caregiver because a psychiatrist in the public system pointed out that patients who cannot recognise an aura cannot act on one, a beauty-salon manager's distrust of local seaweed put ultrafiltration desalting and endotoxin limits into QingdaoAcademy's plan, and a landfill worker of six years gave Hongwen School the handling cost that made local processing a hard constraint. Two further discomforts: the branded cycle acronym is now universal and predicts nothing, with Jilin-China's Social Shaping Loop and GreatBay-SCIE's five-stage framework scoring 2 while plain tables score 4; and awards track legibility rather than consequence, since **KIT** won Inclusivity and GreatBay-SCIE was nominated for Best IHP on evidence that scores 2, while Madrid-UCM, Hongwen School, GYHS and WUXI-DSAS closed loops nobody rewarded.","cards":[{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"Two of three modules were somebody else's idea","body":"Wageningen set out only to degrade trifluoroacetate. Peter Fischer at Aqualab Zuid, one of six labs legally tasked with assessing Dutch drinking water, explained that the compound can only be measured by LC-MS on samples shipped to a central lab, so the bioreactor could not be operated at all without an on-site readout: that created the biosensor module. Bert van der Waal and Peyman Salehian then showed that tenfold reverse-osmosis concentration takes 2.2 micrograms per litre only to 22, against a milligram-per-litre target, which created the capture module. Frank Schoonenberg of Vitens moved the whole deployment target to reverse-osmosis concentrate, and Tue Kjaergaard Nielsen changed the readout to released fluoride because measuring TFA disappearance mistakes adsorption for degradation.","chips":["WageningenUR","Overgrad","Score 4","Utility and lab engineers"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"The conversation that moved sensing out of the cell","body":"GEMS-Taiwan's original design put engineered Bacillus subtilis in the soil with a DesK-DesR system reading temperature directly. On 10 April, Prof. Chen Wen-Liang and bioprocess experts said two things were wrong: the bacteria could not be contained, and biological sensing was neither precise nor controllable enough. Sensing moved out of the cell into electronic sensors and an AIoT model, and a hollow-fibre perfusion bioreactor was built to hold the bacteria in while letting the protectants out. A later public forum with natural-farming advocates, who argued that a crop protected from every stress never builds tolerance, became the specification for the release threshold rather than an objection to be managed.","chips":["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","Score 4","Best IHP winner"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"When the regulator overrules the user","body":"Danny Le Feuvre of the Australian Honey Bee Industry Council and Mike Allerton of Amateur Beekeepers Australia both wanted a persistent living Snodgrassella alvi gut symbiont because it minimises beekeeper labour. Oxford did not simply comply: it took the question to Scottish and Australian regulators and the Soil Association, who pushed the other way, and switched to heat-inactivated dried yeast. The team then stated plainly what that cost — the persistence the beekeepers valued, meaning repeat dosing and more labour. A joint meeting with EPA, FDA and USDA staff stopped them treating the inactivated route as a universal regulatory shortcut, forcing jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction mapping instead.","chips":["Oxford","Undergrad","Score 4","Best IHP nominee"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"A farmer asked for a number","body":"HongKong-JSS built a mercury biosensor with a visible colour readout. Koo's Farm and local wet-market vendors said they wanted numerical readings, not qualitative colour, which is the direct reason the AS7343 14-channel sensor was replaced by a wavelength-resolved Hamamatsu C12880 with a numerical display. Users then reported excessive syringe force on the V1 filter stack, so manual delivery became pump-driven dosing, improving the coefficient of variation from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent. More Happy Farm said plainly that not every farmer wants to own a device, which pushed them to a service model — and after a 195-person demonstration found high perceived confidence, the team separated device status from safety judgement in the interface because confidence is not accuracy.","chips":["HongKong-JSS","High School","Score 4","Non-expert changed hardware"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Method that nobody rewarded","title":"The only team that defined what 'closed' means","body":"Madrid-UCM built a five-rung integration ladder with an explicit closure criterion: a loop counts as closed only when the revised design goes back to the person whose input triggered it and their response produces a further change. They then demonstrated it on materials — Carmen Garcia Payo and Loreto Garcia Fernandez proposed core-shell capsules, the team built them but could not see the internal structure, took that problem back to the same researchers, and got magnetite as an optical tracer plus cryosectioning, which became a wall-thickness and leakage pipeline. Aurelio Hidalgo's point that a single-use biocatalyst is neither economical nor recoverable killed both placeholder designs and moved the enzyme panel onto a reusable solid support. They also document a change they chose not to make, on the grounds that not adding a pathway is a design decision too. No Best IHP nomination.","chips":["Madrid-UCM","Undergrad","Score 4","Not nominated"],"kicker_zh":"沒有被獎勵的做法"},{"kicker":"Format that mostly did not work","title":"The survey that changes your vocabulary","body":"Large public surveys are the most common instrument in the cohort and the least consequential for design. HFI's 434 responses replaced 'genetically modified' with 'engineered' across all materials and rebuilt the education from basics. Peking's 539 respondents named three priorities the team concedes already outlined the finished project. UCAS-China's 419 public respondents and HongKong-HS's 420 produced awareness statistics and workshop plans. The honest version is GHCIS, which found that its price and speed questions branched into samples too small to use and explicitly refused to convert 'within RMB 30' into a product requirement, carrying it forward as a question for frontline users instead.","chips":["HFI","Peking","GHCIS","UCAS-China","Vocabulary, not vector"],"kicker_zh":"大多無效的形式"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Section","Score","What changed"],"rows":[["ABOA","Overgrad","4","Purified enzymes dropped for whole cells on carriers; reactor moved to a side stream"],["Al-Nahrain-IRAQ","Undergrad","4","AI model abandoned for equation-based modelling; lab data entry page added"],["Athens","Overgrad","4","Delivery moved from spray to feed; live phage dropped for a non-replicating enzyme"],["BGCFullerton","High School","4","CIF peptides dropped; regolith mixture plan and model validation changed"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","High School","4","Multivalent antibody replaced by a single monovalent nanobody"],["Cornell","Undergrad","4","Homemade high-voltage supply dropped; hypoxia AND gate added for specificity"],["DTU-Denmark","Overgrad","4","Enzyme step reframed as solvolysis complement; chassis to K. phaffii; docking filter dropped"],["ETH-Zurich","Overgrad","4","Pivot off the Drosophila biopesticide; split-cargo dual targeting invented"],["Eton-College-UK","High School","4","Plasmid backbone changed; reusable reader plus disposable cartridge fixed"],["GCGS","High School","4","VOC module de-scoped; temperature kill switch added, pH switch declined with a reason"],["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","4","Sensing moved out of the cell; perfusion reactor added; proline delivery abandoned"],["GYHS","High School","4","Bond strength replaced by a seven-part requirement set; V2 handling redesigned"],["HFI","High School","4","Lysine-responsive promoter abandoned for constitutive expression"],["HK-Joint-School","High School","4","Goal shifted from fire retardancy to non-toxic, low-smoke; benchmark added"],["HKSSC","High School","4","Kill switch and controlled use; MIC/growth-rate design; pH range from regulator data"],["HKU-HongKong","Unlisted","4","Hypothesis narrowed to partial inflammation modulation; M1/M2 framing dropped"],["HUST-China","Undergrad","4","Reflectin module abandoned entirely for a fashion-waste cellulose route"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","High School","4","Target moved from mineralised calculus to pre-mineralisation biofilm matrix"],["Heidelberg","Undergrad","4","Expression host swapped to a Serratia cassette; engineering retargeted onto GvpC"],["HongKong-HS","High School","4","Toehold switch replaced by HCR; ThT fluorescence replaced by G4/hemin colour"],["HongKong-JSS","High School","4","Colour sensor replaced by spectrometer; syringe replaced by pump dosing"],["Hongwen School","High School","4","IBS claims struck; selection marker changed; near-site processing made a hard constraint"],["ICJFLS","High School","4","Capsule killed for mouthwash/lozenge/gum set; plasmid dropped for chromosomal integration"],["IISER-Kolkata","Unlisted","4","Kill switch rebuilt around a hypochlorite sensor because plants do not use UV"],["KAUST-KSA","Overgrad","4","Dsup added to the chassis; payload reprioritised by real mission conditions"],["LYON","Undergrad","4","All living cells removed from the filter; households ruled out as customers"],["Lambert-GA","High School","4","Nanobodies abandoned for minibinders; target narrowed to the VP3 P-domain"],["MIT-MAHE","Undergrad","4","Target customer moved from fragrance houses to aroma compound manufacturers"],["Madrid-UCM","Undergrad","4","Secretion and consortium killed for immobilised enzymes; containment above performance"],["Marburg","Overgrad","4","5'UTR redesigned so the PPR site and RBS are disconnected; RBS testing dropped"],["McGill","Undergrad","4","Dropped ultra-purification; feedstock moved to fresh tailings; tolling business model"],["McMaster-Canada","Undergrad","4","Oncology and allergy concepts dropped for localised gut-associated systems"],["Muenster-University","Overgrad","4","Prediction pipeline rebuilt with a geometric scoring layer; NLR route dropped"],["NBJF","High School","4","DNA storage device abandoned for the enzymatic-writing bottleneck"],["NFLSHS-CHINA","High School","4","Two plasmids collapsed into one; aqueous formulation killed for oil and capsule"],["NJU-China","Undergrad","4","Recorded associations split from model predictions in every view"],["NUS-Singapore","Undergrad","4","Primary use moved from industrial monitoring to early-stage R&D"],["NYCU-Taiwan","Undergrad","4","Claimed advantages withdrawn after reading a competitor's documentation"],["Oxford","Undergrad","4","Living symbiont chassis dropped for heat-inactivated yeast, with the cost published"],["PSI Korea","High School","4","Auto-exposure disabled and imaging conditions fixed; instrument separated from material"],["Princeton","Undergrad","4","AlphaFold3 cut from the pipeline; IL-6 and amyloid-beta targets dropped"],["QingdaoAcademy","High School","4","One-pot process split in two; pH switch abandoned; desalting and endotoxin control added"],["RDFZ-China","High School","4","Host switched to C41(DE3); metal anchors replaced by on-site stone"],["SEHS","High School","4","Indication moved from liver to gastric cancer; binding re-tested per format"],["SMS-Shenzhen","High School","4","Target customer relocated from front-end recyclers to hydrometallurgical tail streams"],["SUIS-SFLS","High School","4","Deliverable rewritten from finished dressing to characterised protein plus QC records"],["Stanford University","Undergrad","4","Burns dropped for keloids; target moved from prevention to established scars"],["Stockholm","Overgrad","4","Open release abandoned for a sealed reactor sited at the membrane-bioreactor stage"],["TAU-Israel","Overgrad","4","Markers stratified across superficial and deep lesions; biosensor demoted to triage"],["TU Delft","Overgrad","4","Antibiotics dropped for AMPs; pre-coated implant instead of in-theatre paste"],["UAlberta","Undergrad","4","Binding-pocket release abandoned; yeast dropped for E. coli; GFP to mScarlet"],["UCAS-China","Undergrad","4","NKX2-1 cargo dropped for SLPI; repositioned to asthma maintenance"],["UCNZ","Undergrad","4","Distributed plants dropped for one central facility; sustainability claim narrowed"],["UFABC-Brazil","Overgrad","4","Pipetted cell-free reaction replaced by a paper strip; alert routed to a support network"],["UNILausanne","Overgrad","4","Defend strategy kept against the model's own advice; model scope declared the limit"],["UOttawa","Undergrad","4","Target stream moved from bitumen to diesel; pH loop added to the P&ID"],["UZurich","Overgrad","4","Machine-learning plan dropped for established software; root cohesion added to the model"],["Uni-Padua-IT","Undergrad","4","Cold-tolerance module cut; perchlorate genes compartmentalised in heterocysts"],["Vilnius-Lithuania","Undergrad","4","Gel software moved off image classification onto band-distance matching"],["WUXI-DSAS","High School","4","gtdT excised to restore linearity; output changed to a creatinine ratio"],["WageningenUR","Overgrad","4","Biosensor and capture modules created; readout changed to released fluoride"],["William-and-Mary","Undergrad","4","Readout replaced by CFU viability; seawater microcosm experiments added"],["Worldshaper-Shanghai","High School","4","Capacity-building dropped for licensing; sunlight-is-greener claims deleted"],["XJTLU-China","Undergrad","4","Success redefined as soluble protein, not total expression"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","High School","3","Positioning moved from replacement to extra source; patch route added"],["Baltimore","High School","3","Preservation study and patent strategy added; changes peripheral to the build"],["CalPolySLO","Undergrad","3","Survivability testing and a misuse framework added; the build itself unchanged"],["DKU","Undergrad","3","Per-application immunogenicity thresholds and clearer tool output; attribution collective"],["GHCIS","High School","3","Microfluidic format replaced by filter paper, on unnamed industry advice"],["GU Frankfurt","Overgrad","3","Binder accuracy made the governing constraint; biggest change was procedural"],["Kyoto","Undergrad","3","Food themes abandoned and the question reframed; specific changes not itemised"],["Peking","Undergrad","3","Broad-spectrum pesticide and crude biocontrol routes dropped; chain not attributed"],["SDU-Denmark","Overgrad","3","Target moved to reliable low-power generation; no named source"],["SJTU-BioX-Shanghai","Undergrad","3","Repositioned as a post-debridement dressing with physical containment; sources unnamed"],["Toronto","Overgrad","3","Contained bioreactor and close-homology enzymes preferred; stakeholders unnamed"],["UCL","Undergrad","3","Regulatory gap found and a techno-economic model built; the device did not change"],["UPF-Barcelona","Undergrad","3","Central claim shrunk from bulk soil water to a hydration shell at the root"],["ZJU-China","Undergrad","3","Cost weighted more heavily in material design; attribution aggregated"],["ZQT-Nanjing","High School","3","Narrowed from general skincare to barrier repair after a 397-person survey"],["BAID-China","High School","2","Communication depth differentiated by audience; accessibility artefacts revised"],["BNDS-China","High School","2","Workflow discipline borrowed from a peer team; rest is framing"],["BOKU-Vienna","Overgrad","2","Claims key design decisions changed but does not say which"],["CAU-China","Undergrad","2","Need reported from Malawi and Zambia; no design consequence recorded"],["GreatBay-SCIE","High School","2","Slogan changed on stigma grounds; design philosophy only loosely attributed"],["HBUT-China","Undergrad","2","Named virologist fed the risk assessment; no design consequence stated"],["Jilin-China","Undergrad","2","Double-loop reframing of what counts as success; consequences not shown"],["KIT","Overgrad","2","Survey converted into two inclusivity deliverables; science untouched"],["Labi-Taiwan","High School","2","Complements-not-replaces framing and a detects-not-diagnoses statement"],["Mingdao","High School","2","Five honest questions, including a no-project condition; no design change recorded"],["UMA Malaga","Undergrad","2","Question reframed around the diagnostic pathway, not the device"],["UOregon","Overgrad","2","Plant operators confirmed the gap; equity framing shaped, design did not"],["NIS Almaty-Medeu","High School","1","Questions published in advance; no answers or consequences recorded yet"],["Yucai-SZ","High School","1","A 719-response survey tested the premise; no consequence recorded"]]},"method":"Every team in this report is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee, so this is the most decorated tenth of the competition and not a representative sample. Read '64 of 93 closed the loop' as 'closing the loop is normal among teams that win things', not as a statement about iGEM at large. Every team file with any good.ihp content was scored on the four-point rubric from what the file itself states: a 4 required a named stakeholder, a specific thing said, and a change to the build, the deployment, the readout, the safety design or the business model that the file ties to that input. Teams whose only documented consequence was a change of framing, language, education material or evidence package scored 2 or 3 however elaborately the process was branded, and awards were ignored throughout. The rubric cannot verify that a change was made because of the advice rather than attributed to it afterwards, cannot see the wiki behind the summary, and cannot distinguish a thin causal chain from a thin write-up of a thick one. Files continued to land while the scoring ran; all 93 present at the end were read and scored, so the set is complete as of writing but not closed.","scored":93,"kicker_zh":"原創分析"},{"id":"real-world","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"The commercial work that was worth reading argued against itself","title_zh":"值得一讀的商業分析，都在反駁自己","lede":"Across the 2026 field, the teams with credible real-world plans are the ones that published a model showing their own product losing.","lede_zh":"綜觀 2026 年，真實世界計畫最可信的團隊，都公開了一個顯示自家產品輸掉的模型。","body":"Almost every iGEM team produces a business model canvas. Very few produce a number that could have gone against them. The difference is the whole of what separates a credible 2026 commercial section from a template.\n\n**Worldshaper-Shanghai** published a recomputable net-present-value model and reported the result honestly: their own enzyme gives a **negative NPV**. They did not bury it, soften it, or quietly change the discount rate. **BGI-College** did the same with arithmetic instead of finance — a break-even calculation comparing 6.70 against 4.0 mol H₂ per mol glucose disproved the team's own premise, and forced a redesign around byproduct valorisation. **DTU-Denmark** ran a prospective life-cycle assessment in SimaPro with ReCiPe 2016 H and found its enzymatic route emits 2.1 kg CO₂-eq/kg against 1.4 for solvolysis and 0.9 for pyrolysis, with cement co-processing beating them on almost every indicator — then converted each losing indicator into a named engineering target. **Madrid-UCM** published an ISO 14040/44 openLCA result that currently rules against its own technology.\n\n**Stockholm** went furthest. Its safety advisory board killed the open-water release the project was built around, so the team dismantled the venture, retreated to a contained membrane bioreactor on a smaller industrial stream, and made the deliverable **reusable safety infrastructure** instead: an STPA hazard analysis, a nine-system wastewater containment guidebook, and a measurement-uncertainty toolkit. Giving up the product and shipping the method is a result, and it was recognised with the Safety and Security Award.\n\nSet against that, the template is easy to spot once you know the tell: **the cost side is real and the revenue side is fantasy**. ZJU-China itemises equipment at CNY 7.45 million, media, IPTG and labour, and publishes a downloadable cost sheet — genuinely good work — then assumes **100% capture of its serviceable obtainable market** to reach a USD 427 million NPV. The discipline applied to the inputs evaporates at the outputs.\n\nThe high-school tier is not behind here, and in places it is ahead. **SUIS-SFLS** built the only full financial model in the high-school set: capital expenditure of CNY 6.8 and 11.65 million across two scenarios, CNY 71 and 163.5 per litre, 34% against 15.9% margins, break-even years, and the spreadsheets published as downloadable PDFs, on a dual NMPA and ISO 13485 regulatory track. **ICJFLS** works bottom-up from unit economics — RMB 0.8 per dose against RMB 199 retail — with a 745-response survey and a named CDMO. **NFLSHS-CHINA** has a filed and accepted patent on a CsCCD2 mutant, two physical minimum viable products with formula tables, and labels its partnerships as prospective rather than implying they are signed.\n\nThe second thing the credible teams do is **name the stage of each claim**. Baltimore runs Venture Creation Labs OKRs with numeric gates and IRB-approved trilingual surveys, and says plainly that its letters of intent and grants are targets rather than commitments. McGill has a full techno-economic analysis — $11.83 to $20.58 per kg of rare earth oxide, an Ashram project NPV of +USD 51 million, seven sensitivity analyses — an accelerator place, a venture-capital mentor, two letters of support and secured tailings samples, and states that it is not yet incorporated. Nobody is penalised for an early-stage venture. Teams are penalised, correctly, for presenting an aspiration in the grammar of an achievement.\n\nAnd a reminder that not every project should become a company. **HBUT-China**, **WHU-China**, **Squirrel-Beijing** and **BASIS-China** have no venture at all. Their deliverable is infrastructure other teams can use: 34 parts in four independently reusable modules with measurement parts built in and honest terminator read-through annotations; a five-layer characterisation of Neo-IL-2 including surface plasmon resonance and high-passage stability; a tunable bile-acid kill switch with a measured 0.1–0.2 mM threshold compared against real sewage and soil concentrations, plus a published five-step framework for characterising kill switches. That is a real-world contribution with a longer half-life than most business plans.","body_zh":"幾乎每一支 iGEM 團隊都會生出一張商業模式畫布，但很少有團隊生出一個「有可能對自己不利」的數字。而這個差別，就是 2026 年可信的商業章節與樣板之間的全部距離。\n\n**Worldshaper-Shanghai** 公開了一個可重新計算的淨現值模型，並誠實報告結果：他們自己的酵素得出**負的 NPV**。他們沒有把它藏起來、淡化，也沒有偷偷調整折現率。**BGI-College** 做了同樣的事，只是用算術而非財務——一個比較 6.70 與 4.0 mol H₂／mol 葡萄糖的損益兩平計算，推翻了團隊自己的前提，迫使他們圍繞副產物加值重新設計。**DTU-Denmark** 以 SimaPro 搭配 ReCiPe 2016 H 做了前瞻性生命週期評估，發現自家的酵素路線排放 2.1 kg CO₂-eq/kg，而溶劑解為 1.4、熱解為 0.9，水泥共處理在幾乎每一項指標上都勝過他們——然後把每一項輸掉的指標轉化為一個具名的工程目標。**Madrid-UCM** 則公開了一份 ISO 14040/44 的 openLCA 結果，而該結果目前判定對他們自己的技術不利。\n\n**Stockholm** 走得最遠。他們的安全諮詢委員會否決了整個專案賴以成立的開放水域釋放，於是團隊拆掉了這個創業構想，退回到處理較小工業廢流的密閉式膜生物反應器，並把產出改成**可重複使用的安全基礎設施**：一份 STPA 危害分析、一本涵蓋九種系統的廢水圍堵指南，以及一套量測不確定度工具包。放棄產品、交付方法，本身就是一種成果，而它拿下了安全與保安獎。\n\n對照之下，樣板一旦知道徵兆就很好認：**成本端是真的，營收端是幻想**。ZJU-China 列出 7,450 萬人民幣的設備、培養基、IPTG 與人力，還公開可下載的成本表——這是扎實的工作——接著假設**100% 拿下其可服務可獲得市場**，得出 4.27 億美元的 NPV。用在投入端的紀律，到了產出端就蒸發了。\n\n高中組在這件事上並不落後，有些地方甚至領先。**SUIS-SFLS** 做出高中組唯一一份完整的財務模型：兩種情境下 680 萬與 1,165 萬人民幣的資本支出、每公升 71 元與 163.5 元、34% 對 15.9% 的毛利率、損益兩平年份，試算表以可下載 PDF 公開，並走 NMPA 與 ISO 13485 雙軌法規路徑。**ICJFLS** 從單位經濟由下而上推算——每劑 0.8 人民幣對零售價 199 元——搭配 745 份問卷與一家具名的 CDMO。**NFLSHS-CHINA** 則有一件已提出並受理的 CsCCD2 突變體專利、兩個附配方表的實體最小可行產品，而且把合作關係標示為「潛在」，不暗示已經簽約。\n\n可信團隊做的第二件事，是**標明每一項主張所處的階段**。Baltimore 以 Venture Creation Labs 的 OKR 搭配量化關卡運作，做了經 IRB 核准的三語問卷，並直說他們的意向書與補助都只是目標，不是承諾。McGill 有完整的技術經濟分析——每公斤稀土氧化物 11.83 至 20.58 美元、Ashram 專案淨現值 +5,100 萬美元、七項敏感度分析——有加速器席位、創投導師、兩封支持信與已取得的尾礦樣本，並載明尚未完成公司設立。沒有人會因為創業處於早期而被扣分；被扣分的——而且理所當然——是用「已完成」的文法去陳述一個「想達成」的願望。\n\n最後提醒：不是每一個專案都該變成公司。**HBUT-China**、**WHU-China**、**Squirrel-Beijing** 與 **BASIS-China** 根本沒有創業規劃。他們的產出是其他團隊可以使用的基礎設施：34 個分屬四個可獨立重用模組的元件，內建量測用元件，並誠實註記終止子讀通問題；Neo-IL-2 的五層次表徵，含表面電漿共振與高代次穩定性；一個可調控的膽酸自殺開關，量測到 0.1–0.2 mM 的閾值並與真實污水及土壤濃度對照，外加一套已發表的自殺開關五步驟表徵框架。這是一種真實世界的貢獻，而且半衰期比多數商業計畫書都長。","cards":[{"kicker":"The strongest move","title":"Publish the model that says no","title_zh":"公開那個說「不」的模型","body":"Worldshaper-Shanghai's recomputable NPV model finds their own enzyme gives a negative NPV, and says so. DTU-Denmark's prospective LCA finds cement co-processing beats their enzymatic route on almost every indicator, then turns each losing indicator into an engineering target. Madrid-UCM's ISO 14040/44 assessment currently rules against its own technology. A model that could only ever have agreed with you is not evidence.","body_zh":"Worldshaper-Shanghai 可重算的 NPV 模型得出自家酵素為負 NPV，而他們照實寫出來。DTU-Denmark 的前瞻性 LCA 發現水泥共處理在幾乎每項指標上都勝過他們的酵素路線，於是把每一項輸掉的指標轉成工程目標。Madrid-UCM 的 ISO 14040/44 評估目前判定對自家技術不利。一個只可能同意你的模型，不是證據。","chips":["negative NPV, published","LCA that rules against you"],"kicker_zh":"最強的一步"},{"kicker":"The tell","title":"Real costs, fantasy revenue","title_zh":"真實的成本，幻想的營收","body":"ZJU-China itemises CNY 7.45 million of equipment, media, IPTG and labour and publishes a downloadable cost sheet — then assumes 100% capture of its serviceable obtainable market to reach a USD 427 million NPV. This is the most common failure mode in iGEM commercial sections: rigour on the inputs, where the team has data, and none on the outputs, where it does not.","body_zh":"ZJU-China 逐項列出 7,450 萬人民幣的設備、培養基、IPTG 與人力，還公開可下載的成本表——接著假設 100% 拿下可服務可獲得市場，得出 4.27 億美元的 NPV。這是 iGEM 商業章節最常見的失敗模式：在團隊有資料的投入端講究嚴謹，在沒有資料的產出端完全放棄。","chips":["100% SOM capture"],"kicker_zh":"破綻"},{"kicker":"The result that looks like a failure","title":"Stockholm dismantled its own venture","title_zh":"Stockholm 拆掉了自己的創業計畫","body":"A safety advisory board killed the open-water release the project was built on. Rather than argue, the team retreated to a contained membrane bioreactor on a smaller stream and shipped reusable safety infrastructure instead — an STPA hazard analysis, a nine-system wastewater containment guidebook, a measurement-uncertainty toolkit. It won the Safety and Security Award. Giving up the product and publishing the method is a result.","body_zh":"安全諮詢委員會否決了這個專案賴以成立的開放水域釋放。團隊沒有爭辯，而是退回到處理較小廢流的密閉式膜生物反應器，改為交付可重複使用的安全基礎設施——STPA 危害分析、涵蓋九種系統的廢水圍堵指南、量測不確定度工具包。它拿下了安全與保安獎。放棄產品、公開方法，本身就是成果。","chips":["Safety and Security Award"],"kicker_zh":"看起來像失敗的成果"},{"kicker":"High school, ahead","title":"SUIS-SFLS built the only full financial model in its tier","title_zh":"SUIS-SFLS 做出該組唯一一份完整財務模型","body":"Capital expenditure of CNY 6.8 and 11.65 million across two scenarios, CNY 71 and 163.5 per litre, 34% against 15.9% margins, break-even years, spreadsheets published as downloadable PDFs, on a dual NMPA and ISO 13485 track. ICJFLS works bottom-up from RMB 0.8 per dose against RMB 199 retail with a named CDMO. The census found high-school teams do more techno-economic analysis than undergraduates; this is what that looks like up close.","body_zh":"兩種情境下 680 萬與 1,165 萬人民幣的資本支出、每公升 71 元與 163.5 元、34% 對 15.9% 的毛利率、損益兩平年份，試算表以可下載 PDF 公開，並走 NMPA 與 ISO 13485 雙軌。ICJFLS 則由下而上從每劑 0.8 人民幣對零售價 199 元推算，並列出具名的 CDMO。技術普查發現高中隊伍做的技術經濟分析比大學部還多；放大來看就是這個樣子。","chips":["capex, margins, break-even","NMPA + ISO 13485"],"kicker_zh":"高中組，領先"},{"kicker":"The habit","title":"Name the stage of every claim","title_zh":"標明每一項主張所處的階段","body":"Baltimore says plainly that its letters of intent and grants are targets, not commitments. McGill has a full techno-economic analysis, an accelerator place, a VC mentor, two letters of support and secured tailings samples — and states it is not yet incorporated. NFLSHS-CHINA labels its partnerships prospective. Nobody is penalised for being early. Teams are penalised for writing an aspiration in the grammar of an achievement.","body_zh":"Baltimore 直說他們的意向書與補助都只是目標，不是承諾。McGill 有完整的技術經濟分析、加速器席位、創投導師、兩封支持信與已取得的尾礦樣本——並載明尚未完成公司設立。NFLSHS-CHINA 把合作關係標示為潛在。沒有人會因為處於早期而被扣分；被扣分的是用「已完成」的文法去寫一個「想達成」的願望。","chips":["early is fine","overclaiming is not"],"kicker_zh":"習慣"},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"Not every project should become a company","title_zh":"不是每個專案都該變成公司","body":"HBUT-China, WHU-China, Squirrel-Beijing and BASIS-China have no venture at all. They shipped infrastructure instead — 34 parts in four reusable modules with measurement parts built in, a five-layer Neo-IL-2 characterisation, a tunable kill switch with a measured 0.1–0.2 mM threshold checked against real sewage concentrations, and a published five-step framework for characterising kill switches. For an institution building a reputation, that has a longer half-life than a business plan.","body_zh":"HBUT-China、WHU-China、Squirrel-Beijing 與 BASIS-China 完全沒有創業規劃。他們交付的是基礎設施——34 個分屬四個可重用模組、內建量測元件的零件；Neo-IL-2 的五層次表徵；一個量測到 0.1–0.2 mM 閾值、並與真實污水濃度對照的可調控自殺開關；以及一套已發表的自殺開關五步驟表徵框架。對一個正在建立聲譽的機構而言，這些東西的半衰期比商業計畫書長得多。","chips":["parts outlive plans"],"kicker_zh":"給 GEMS"}],"method":"Drawn from the realWorld fields of the team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Financial figures are the teams' own and are not independently audited; where a team's assumptions looked unsupported that is noted as our reading, not as a finding of error. Teams that published a model unfavourable to themselves are over-represented here because that is exactly what the analysis is about — it is not a claim that most 2026 teams did so.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告團隊檔案中的 realWorld 欄位，每一份都來自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。財務數字為各隊自報且未經獨立查核；凡判斷某隊假設缺乏支撐之處，均屬我們的閱讀判斷，而非認定其有誤。公開了對自己不利之模型的團隊在此被過度呈現，因為那正是本篇分析的主題——這並不表示 2026 年多數團隊都這麼做。","kicker_zh":"原創分析"},{"id":"software-afterlife","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Does award-winning iGEM software survive the Jamboree?","lede":"Of 21 software tools released by award-winning iGEM 2026 teams, 8 are live and usable by a stranger today, 11 are source-only, and 2 have already gone dark.","body":"**Eight of twenty-one.** That is the honest base rate for award-winning iGEM 2026 software that a stranger can open and use today, four weeks after the Jamboree. Eleven more are source-only: the code is public, populated and often genuinely good, but using it means cloning a repository and running Docker. Two are already dead — Vilnius-Lithuania's Ladder Detector now answers \"This service has been suspended by its owner\" at ladder-detector.onrender.com, and TAU-Israel's CERNAL fails to resolve at both cernal.app and cernal.duckdns.org, the two addresses its own wiki advertises.\n\nThe striking thing is that nothing is a stub. Every repository checked was populated with real code, a README and a licence. iGEM's mandatory GitLab deposit has solved the empty-repo problem completely. What it has not solved, and cannot, is hosting: the competition requires you to publish source, and publishing source is where most teams stop.\n\nThe live ones have one habit in common, and it is not budget. **They bought a domain and pointed it at a running backend before the wiki freeze, then wrote the wiki around a URL rather than around an install command.** NJU-China's Atlas sits on starase-atlas.org, XJTLU-Software's AMPilot on ampilotlab.com, Toronto's PETadex on petadex.net, Stanford's RADAR-Scout on Vercel. Two of the eight are high-school teams running real inference in public: GHCIS's ARGUS answers `{\"status\":\"ready\"}` at argus.ucuv.dpdns.org, and HK-Joint-School's PyroForge reports `models_ready: true, esm_ready: true` — an ESM protein model loaded and serving, from a school team.\n\nThe source-only group is not lazy; it is mostly careful. ETH-Zurich's deCISion ships 28 CI-tested checks, a Docker build and an MIT licence. UMA Malaga's Diana has a 10 GB reproducible Docker stack and a BIOLOGICAL_REPORT.md mapping each biological step to code. Uni-Padua-IT's ReTIsigner is a thoughtful fork of a published tool, Apache 2.0, one `docker run` from working. These teams decided, often explicitly and for defensible reasons — cost, patient data, a 4 GB index — that local execution was the right call. The cost is simply that nobody will ever casually try them.\n\nTwo teams published a live URL that is not the tool, and both said so honestly. UMA Malaga's diana-grna-designer-7723f5.igem.wiki opens with \"Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.\" GU Frankfurt's HUSH page says \"This page shows its web app in action\" and then presents a clickable mockup of screenshots. Judges reward the appearance of a deployed tool, so the gap between a demo and a deployment is exactly where a link check gets fooled.\n\nOutside use is the bleakest column. Across every GitLab repository examined the star count is zero, the fork count is zero, and the last commit falls in the October freeze window — with one exception, DKU's pepticraft-2, touched on 5 November. Uni-Padua-IT published an open call on 9 August offering to codon-optimise any team's sequence, received no replies, and reported that on their wiki. The only genuine external-adoption signal found anywhere was on Stanford's SynBase, which displays \"837 learners\" — and that is a teaching platform, not a research tool.\n\nOne more caution for anyone citing datasets as deliverables. Toronto's PETadex front end is live and excellent, but the 23.8 GB Zenodo deposit its wiki cites, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986, returns 404, and a Zenodo search for \"petadex\" returns zero records. The web app survived; the archival half of the release did not.\n\nFor GEMS the lesson is narrow and cheap. Shipping a tool outsiders use is achievable — eight teams did it, including two high schools — but it is a hosting decision, not a coding decision, and it has to be made months before the wiki freeze. The teams that got there treated the public URL as the deliverable and the repository as the backup. The ones that did not now own excellent code that nobody will run.","cards":[{"kicker":"Best in class","title":"AMPilot — the only tool with a working public API","body":"XJTLU-Software's antimicrobial-peptide workbench at ampilotlab.com opens in guest mode with no account, and its /api/v1 routes are documented in a published OpenAPI 3.1 spec. A live call to /api/v1/corpus/search returned real literature evidence with provenance, licence and retrieval date attached — no key, no sign-up. The spec states the API is deterministic, stateless and calls no language model, which is what makes it safe for someone else to build on. It is the clearest example this year of a team designing for a second user rather than a judge.","chips":["alive","XJTLU-Software","public API","guest mode","OpenAPI 3.1"],"kicker_zh":"同類最佳"},{"kicker":"Proof it is not a budget problem","title":"Two high-school teams out-shipped most universities","body":"GHCIS's ARGUS runs a real backend at argus.ucuv.dpdns.org — its /api/ready endpoint answers with JSON, not a static shell — alongside a Docker and a native Node deploy path, role-based access and SQLite persistence. HK-Joint-School's PyroForge serves protein thermostability prediction at pyroforge.26650078.xyz with /health reporting ESM models loaded and ready. Both URLs are reachable right now. Neither team had a university budget; they had a cheap domain and a decision to host.","chips":["alive","GHCIS","HK-Joint-School","high school","real backend"],"kicker_zh":"證明這不是預算問題"},{"kicker":"The cautionary tale","title":"Vilnius deployed, then switched it off","body":"Ladder Detector automates gel-image annotation, a genuinely unglamorous and genuinely useful job, and Vilnius-Lithuania did the right thing by deploying it publicly. The URL on their wiki, ladder-detector.onrender.com, now returns HTTP 503 and the text \"This service has been suspended by its owner.\" The Apache-2.0 source is intact on GitLab and still runs via docker compose, so the work is not lost — but every citation of that wiki link now points at a dead page. A free hosting tier is a deadline, not a deployment.","chips":["gone","Vilnius-Lithuania","503 suspended","source survives"],"kicker_zh":"前車之鑑"},{"kicker":"Honest about the gap","title":"Diana and HUSH publish a URL that is not the tool","body":"UMA Malaga's live site opens with a disclaimer: \"Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.\" It publishes unedited CLI output with the commit hash, Docker image digest and tool versions recorded — excellent reproducibility practice, but not a service. GU Frankfurt's HUSH page likewise says it \"shows its web app in action\" and then walks through a mockup of screenshots. Both are more honest than most, and both are exactly why a 200 response proves nothing until you read the page.","chips":["source-only","UMA Malaga","GU Frankfurt","demo not deployment"],"kicker_zh":"誠實面對落差"},{"kicker":"Good code, no front door","title":"ETH-Zurich's deCISion is the best source-only release","body":"The Best Software winner for Overgrad ships MIT-licensed with a web interface, a JSON API, a CLI, 28 automated tests on every push through GitLab CI, a Docker build, a CITATION.cff and a demo video. It exports FASTA, GenBank and SBOL3 and takes any .pdb or .cif structure, so it would work on someone else's data without modification. The only address on the wiki is localhost:4173. Everything needed to deploy it exists in the repository; nobody deployed it.","chips":["source-only","ETH-Zurich","MIT","CI + Docker","localhost only"],"kicker_zh":"程式很好，沒有入口"},{"kicker":"Check the whole release","title":"Toronto's app is live; its dataset DOI is not","body":"PETadex at petadex.net is one of the strongest tools of the year: a sharded DIAMOND search over a 298.7M-sequence corpus, with worked examples loaded and ready to run, nothing to install. But the wiki cites a 23.8 GB Zenodo deposit at doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986, and that DOI returns 404 — a Zenodo API search for \"petadex\" finds zero records. The interactive half survived and the archival half did not, which is the opposite of what long-term preservation is supposed to deliver.","chips":["alive","Toronto","petadex.net","Zenodo DOI 404"],"kicker_zh":"檢查整個釋出"}],"table":{"head":["Tool","Team","Status","Live URL / repo","Reusable on other data?"],"rows":[["AMPilot","XJTLU-Software","alive","https://ampilotlab.com","yes"],["ARGUS","GHCIS","alive","https://argus.ucuv.dpdns.org/client/","yes"],["Atlas COMPASS + EDGE","NJU-China","alive","https://www.starase-atlas.org/","partly"],["PETadex sequence search","Toronto","alive","https://petadex.net/search","yes"],["PyroForge","HK-Joint-School","alive","https://pyroforge.26650078.xyz/","yes"],["PeptiCraft","DKU","alive","https://pepticraft.pages.dev","partly"],["RADAR-Scout","Stanford University","alive","https://radar-scout.vercel.app/","partly"],["SynBase","Stanford University","alive","https://synbase.web.app/home.html","n/a (curriculum)"],["deCISion","ETH-Zurich","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/decision","yes"],["OpenSplitProtein","ETH-Zurich","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/opensplitprotein","yes"],["ReTIsigner","Uni-Padua-IT","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uni-padua-it/retisigner-svelte","yes"],["RK4 solver","UPF-Barcelona","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","yes"],["iGEMforge","UPF-Barcelona","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","partly"],["NetFlux","MIT-MAHE","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux","yes"],["Diana gRNA designer","UMA Malaga","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uma-malaga/diana-grna-designer","yes"],["HUSH","GU Frankfurt","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gu-frankfurt/hush","yes"],["PRINCE","Lambert-GA","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-webapp","yes"],["catmaOS","XJTLU-China","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/xjtlu-china/software","partly"],["Bioreactor digital twin","GEMS-Taiwan","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gems-taiwan/digital-twin","no"],["Ladder Detector","Vilnius-Lithuania","gone","ladder-detector.onrender.com (503 suspended)","yes, if self-hosted"],["CERNAL","TAU-Israel","gone","cernal.app + cernal.duckdns.org (both unresolvable)","partly, if self-hosted"],["Electrospinner (no software)","Cornell","n/a","CAD, BOM and manuals only","n/a"],["Bioreactor stack (no software)","KAUST-KSA","n/a","gitlab.igem.org/2026/kaust-ksa","n/a"]]},"checklist":["Buy a domain and deploy the tool publicly before the wiki freeze, not after it — every tool that is alive today was hosted on freeze day.","Put a clickable URL at the top of the software page; if the only address on the page is localhost, assume nobody outside the team will ever run it.","Let strangers in without an account — guest mode or a no-key API. CERNAL gated behind a lab login is dead; AMPilot's keyless API still answers.","Pay for hosting that outlives the free tier, and check the URL again a month after the Jamboree. Vilnius's deployment lasted weeks.","Expose a documented HTTP API with an OpenAPI spec alongside the UI, so the tool can be a step in someone else's pipeline rather than a destination.","Ship a health endpoint that returns real JSON, so anyone — including a judge or a reviewer — can prove the backend is running and not a static shell.","Accept standard inputs (FASTA, GenBank, SBML, .pdb/.cif) and export standard outputs (SBOL, GenBank, CSV); hard-wiring the tool to your own chassis caps its audience at your team.","Never present a mockup or saved output as the running tool — and if you do publish saved results, label them as plainly as UMA Malaga did.","Verify every archival DOI resolves before you cite it; Toronto's 23.8 GB Zenodo deposit 404s while the web app it supports stays up.","Recruit one outside user and record what they did. Across all 21 tools the only external-adoption number found anywhere was SynBase's 837 learners; stars and forks were zero everywhere."],"method":"Starting from the 2026 Best Software winners and nominees, the Best Software & AI winners and nominees, and the Best Model and Best Hardware winners, every tool's wiki software page was read (via curl where server-rendered, via the browser pane for client-rendered SPAs), every GitLab and GitHub repository was queried through the GitLab API for file tree, licence, stars, forks and last-commit date, and every candidate deployment was first checked with curl and then opened in a browser and read, because a 200 from an SPA catch-all route proves nothing — starase-atlas.org returns its index page for any /api path, so apparent API endpoints had to be inspected by content. Where a backend health endpoint existed it was called directly (ARGUS /api/ready, PyroForge /health, AMPilot /api/v1/corpus/search, which returned real data). A link check cannot tell you whether the science is correct, whether the tool gives sensible answers on data it has not seen, whether the maintainers intend to keep paying for hosting, or whether anyone is actually using it — zero stars and zero forks mean no public signal, not necessarily no users. Cornell and KAUST-KSA released no standalone software and are listed but excluded from the base rate; TAU-Israel, HK-Joint-School, DKU and XJTLU-Software had no local research file, so their tools were identified from their wikis directly.","baseRate":{"checked":21,"alive":8,"sourceOnly":11,"stub":0,"gone":2},"kicker_zh":"原創分析"},{"id":"taiwan-cohort","tab":"teams","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Taiwan at iGEM 2026","lede":"Taiwan fielded thirteen competing teams in 2026 and won six awards, more than any territory in East Asia except China, but every technical award came from the high-school tier and the island is invisible in parts, software and collegiate modelling.","body":"Taiwan registered fifteen entries with iGEM in 2026 and thirteen of them competed — eight high-school, four undergraduate, one overgraduate — returning **eight golds, five silvers and no bronzes**, one Top 10 place, six outright award wins and seven further nominations. The wins were GEMS-Taiwan's Best Measurement, Best Hardware and Best Integrated Human Practices, Labi-Taiwan's peer-voted iGEMers Prize, NYCU-Taiwan's Best Project Promotion Video and NCKU-Tainan's Best Infectious Diseases Project; the nominations added Mingdao for Model, NCKU-Tainan for Hardware, NTHU for Food & Nutrition, Labi-Taiwan for Measurement, and GEMS-Taiwan for Presentation, Wiki and Best Village Project. Against the region that is strong in volume and weak in altitude: China fielded 176 competing teams for 24 wins and five Top 10 places, Hong Kong 16 for three wins, three Top 10 places and the high-school Grand Prize first runner-up in HongKong-JSS, Japan seven for nine nominations and no wins, Korea six for none and Singapore four for none. Taiwan therefore out-won Hong Kong six to three on fewer teams and was the only territory outside China to win more than once, but it took a single Top 10 and placed nothing in any Grand Prize at any tier.\n\nThe strength is **instrumentation**: six of the thirteen teams built and documented a device — GEMS-Taiwan's hollow-fibre perfusion bioreactor and two in-line photometers, NCKU-Tainan's CAPTURE-Screen fluorescence reader at US$54–161 against the US$3,500 open-source plate reader it substitutes, NTHU's four-channel frequency-tagged reader with digital lock-in detection, NTHU Taiwan's open-source moving-bed biofilm reactor, Mingdao's single-frame fermentor and Labi-Taiwan's portable electrochemical reader — with human practices and communication a clear second, carrying three of the six wins. The weakness is just as sharply defined: **not one Taiwanese nomination in any of the four parts awards, and none in Best Software**, where even Hong Kong managed one through HK-Joint-School, despite GEMS-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan and NYCU-Taiwan all releasing licensed code; Best Model appears once, at high-school level, for Mingdao; and the collegiate tier produced no technical special award at all, NYCU-Taiwan's win being a video and NCKU-Tainan's a village category. The clearest symptom is NTHU Taiwan's CatharSys, whose four models dropped a screening factor on a predicted 6% separation, reversed an enzyme-engineering plan when formaldehyde was projected to five times chassis tolerance, stated a falsifiable prediction before the build and reversed a nozzle geometry on first-principles hydraulics — and which won a gold medal and nothing else.\n\nGEMS-Taiwan's three wins and Top 10 place are the island's best result of the year, and they were earned on provenance rather than biology: an input ledger marking every number measured, cited or modelled, a growth rate pre-registered on 1 October and later scored at 0.286 ± 0.010 h⁻¹, and an autoencoder that named a failing photometer 26.7 hours before the channel died. Measured against the collegiate Top 10 sections the dry lab is thin in four named places — there is no inferential statistics, the central secreted-activity figure standing at **n = 1, 7.25 mU/mL, below quantitation** with two induction runs disagreeing on the sign, where NCKU-Tainan a tier up fits mixed models with plate as a random intercept and holds out a treatment to predict; the entire control architecture rests on a published CcaSR Hill curve assumed valid at 20 L although every induction ran at a single light intensity, so nothing in the project tests its own transfer function; the digital twin is an admitted digital shadow, replaying recorded runs with a person making every decision and green-light induction not integrated; and the economics are negative on the team's own numbers, 68 years to payback at perfect efficacy against a partner's 4.9. The step up needs depth in three places rather than more scope: replication and intervals on the central claim with a pre-registered **effect size** rather than a pre-registered growth rate; an in-house CcaSR dose–response across light intensities and scales in absolute fluorescein-calibrated units, which would simultaneously turn 35 contributed SubtiToolKit parts into a collection with the transfer curves a parts award actually rewards; and a twin that controls a run instead of replaying one, with one external software user whose complaints are written down.\n\nThe collaboration map begins with an uncomfortable fact: **GEMS-Taiwan is not in the island's network**. NYCU-Taiwan hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up at its Bo-Ai campus on 27 July for 53 students and advisors from NYCU-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, HIA-Taiwan, VIS and WIST, and NCKU-Tainan's collaboration page adds Mingdao, CCU-Taiwan and NTHU — while neither GEMS-Taiwan nor Labi-Taiwan appears on either list and the GEMS wiki carries no collaboration page at all. The partners therefore follow from complementarity, not goodwill: NTHU Taiwan shares the *Bacillus subtilis* chassis and the open-hardware habit, NCKU-Tainan holds the statistics and the cheap reader, CCU-Taiwan works the rice leafroller on the same crop and the same island, NTHU's AeroSense group has the cohort's deepest computation and admits its decoder was validated on external metal-oxide sensor datasets rather than its own cells, Labi-Taiwan is the only other high-school programme with a real computational stack, and NYCU-Taiwan convenes.\n\nTaiwan's state-backed push is manufacturing-led — the Taiwan Bio-Manufacturing Corporation broke ground on a 15,000 m² GMP facility in Hsinchu Biomedical Science Park in June 2025 with operations from Q2 2026 including Taiwan's first GMP mRNA capability, biomedicine sits inside the 5+2 Innovative Industries Plan, a 33-company delegation went to BIO 2026, and this research found no Taiwan-specific synthetic-biology design programme or funding figure at all. Singapore and Israel are funding precisely that missing layer, with DayOne launching Singapore's first biological data centre prototype in August 2026 and Israel's Innovation Authority committing roughly NIS 70 million in July 2026 to national infrastructure for AI models built on biological data. The 2026 cohort is both the evidence of the gap and the evidence that it can be filled: thirteen teams, six instruments built, zero parts nominations, zero software nominations. GEMS should position itself as Taiwan's dry-lab pipeline rather than as a smaller wet lab, and say so to the Biotechnology and Pharmaceutical Industries Promotion Office and the Ministry of Economic Affairs with Singapore and Israel named as the comparison, to TBMC in Hsinchu as it ramps twenty minutes from NYCU and both NTHU teams, and to the Industrial Technology Research Institute, where NTHU Taiwan already holds a working relationship GEMS would not have to build from scratch.","cards":[{"kicker":"High School · Taipei · id 6072","title":"GEMS-Taiwan — ReLEAF","body":"An optogenetic Bacillus subtilis WB800 bioreactor that reads field sensors and weather forecasts, sets a green-light dose through the CcaSR two-component system and secretes plant-protective proteins beside a Taiwanese paddy. Taiwan's only Top 10 place in 2026 and the island's only triple winner: Best Measurement, Best Hardware and Best Integrated Human Practices, plus nominations for Presentation, Wiki and Best Village Project. The award case rests on provenance rather than biology — a pre-registered growth rate scored after the fact, an autoencoder that named a failing photometer 26.7 hours early, an input ledger marking every number measured, cited or modelled, and a wiki that withdraws its own claims. The hole is that the published CcaSR transfer function the whole control architecture depends on was assumed, never measured, and the central activity figure is n = 1 below quantitation.","chips":["Gold","Top 10","3 wins","Hardware","Measurement","IHP","B. subtilis"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taipei · id 6072"},{"kicker":"High School · Taoyuan · id 6511","title":"Labi-Taiwan — BlueCatcher","body":"A nucleic-acid biosensor for major depressive disorder, built by Labi Education, the programme formerly entered as Taipei-KCISLK. The dry lab is the most data-heavy of any Taiwanese high-school team: differential expression, miRNA–mRNA networks, GSEA and WGCNA narrowed 2,656 mature miRNAs to sixteen candidates and then to miR-124-3p as the first engineering target, with machine learning used to prioritise three-way-junction probes and toehold switches, and thermodynamic and kinetic modelling behind the readout. It won the iGEMers Prize, the award the other teams vote for, and was nominated for Best Measurement on a portable electrochemical reader. Like GEMS, it is a Taipei-area commercial-organiser programme and appears on no other Taiwanese team's collaboration page.","chips":["Gold","iGEMers Prize","Measurement nominee","miRNA","ML","electrochemical"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taoyuan · id 6511"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Hsinchu · id 6306","title":"NYCU-Taiwan — BITE","body":"A modular food-safety biosensor combining magnetic-bead DNA enrichment, CRISPR-Cas12a recognition and G4–hemin colorimetric readout against synthetic DNA from the Salmonella enterica invA region. The dry lab is organised as SeekProbe_Designer for capture-probe design plus a four-layer model stack from bead capture through Cas12a activation and hairpin-G4 colour to end-to-end prediction, with a Y-shaped multi-chamber device concept. It won Best Project Promotion Video — the island's only collegiate win outside a village category — on a silver medal, which is the gap between communication and technical recognition in one team. NYCU is also the convening institution: it hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up for 53 people from five teams and built the exchange website behind it.","chips":["Silver","Best Promotion Video","Cas12a","Meet-Up host","food safety"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Hsinchu · id 6306"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Tainan · id 6379","title":"NCKU-Tainan — Capture","body":"Two engineered E. coli systems reading the same Pseudomonas aeruginosa quorum-sensing signal: one reports AHL as fluorescence, one deploys aptamers to sponge it out of circulation, aimed at healthcare-associated infection in Taiwanese intensive care. It won Best Infectious Diseases Project and was nominated for Best Hardware for CAPTURE-Screen, a single-cuvette fluorescence reader at US$54–161 against US$3,500 for the plate reader it substitutes, paired with LasReader for 4PL calibration with approximate 95% intervals. The statistics are the best in the Taiwanese cohort — mixed models with plate as a random intercept, geometric-mean ratio effect sizes, and the Cb-2 treatment held out and then predicted. It is also the island's mentoring spine, having run a session for Mingdao in March with three of its own members as Mingdao alumni.","chips":["Gold","Infectious Diseases win","Hardware nominee","US$54 reader","mixed models"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Tainan · id 6379"},{"kicker":"Overgrad · Hsinchu · id 6460","title":"NTHU — AeroSense","body":"A biohybrid olfactory platform: Drosophila odorant receptors with ORCO in HEK293 cells, GCaMP6f fluorescence reporting, a four-channel frequency-tagged optical reader with digital lock-in processing, and a fly-inspired network for decoding odour patterns, aimed at early fungal-risk screening in stored bananas. This is the deepest computational work in the Taiwanese cohort — PCA and projection-neuron coding, measured infrared and quantum-vibration features, an OpenPOM comparison, mutation-robustness and cross-species transfer tests, and molecular-dynamics pocket-entry studies. Nominated for Best Food & Nutrition Project and nothing else. The team states its own limit plainly: the decoder was evaluated on external metal-oxide sensor datasets, not on its own cells.","chips":["Gold","Food & Nutrition nominee","GCaMP6f","neural decoder","lock-in optics"],"kicker_zh":"研究生組 · Hsinchu · id 6460"},{"kicker":"High School · Taichung · id 6105","title":"Mingdao — Waste-to-Watt","body":"Laminated paper food containers from a 7,000-student campus turned into bioethanol by simultaneous saccharification and fermentation, with Zymomonas mobilis acting as a glucose sink so that BglA β-glucosidase never becomes product-inhibited and cellulase never sees accumulating cellobiose. Nominated for Best Model on three stacked models — enzyme-inhibition kinetics characterised under fermentation-compatible conditions rather than the thermophilic optimum, Monod growth for Z. mobilis, and a coupled ODE comparing closed and open systems. The hardware is a single 45 × 45 × 60 cm frame carrying shredding, hydrolysis, fermentation and distillation with the vessel riding to the distillation station on its own hotplate, so the mixture is never transferred. The clearest high-school modelling case in Taiwan after GEMS, and the only Taiwanese Best Model nomination at any tier.","chips":["Gold","Best Model nominee","SSF","coupled ODE","fermentor"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taichung · id 6105"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Hsinchu · id 6416 — not on the briefed list","title":"NTHU Taiwan — CatharSys","body":"A second, separate National Tsing Hua University team, distinct from the overgraduate NTHU entry: engineered Bacillus subtilis forming biofilms on suspended carriers in a moving-bed reactor to treat TMAH and trimethylamine waste from Hsinchu's semiconductor lithography lines. Four models, and each one changed a decision — dissolved oxygen was dropped from the screen at a predicted 6% separation below flask noise, strengthening the bottleneck enzyme alone was shown to drive formaldehyde to five times chassis tolerance so a matched hxlAB upregulation was carried instead, a biofilm model stated a falsifiable prediction before the build, and first-principles hydraulics reversed a nozzle geometry for the pump already bought. CathaBench, its three-tank open-source benchtop MBBR with ESP32 control and an offline Wi-Fi dashboard, was iterated on feedback from ITRI and industry. Gold medal, zero nominations — on this evidence the most under-recognised dry lab in Taiwan in 2026, and the closest technical match to GEMS.","chips":["Gold","no awards","B. subtilis","MBBR","ITRI","semiconductor waste"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Hsinchu · id 6416 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Chiayi · id 6408 — not on the briefed list","title":"CCU-Taiwan — NoFold","body":"National Chung Cheng University against the rice leafroller, Cnaphalocrocis medinalis, which folds a rice leaf and eats it from inside and is described as a predominant foliage feeder across Asian rice ecosystems. The framing is the same economic argument GEMS makes: only about 12% of world rice crosses a border, so an Asian yield loss cannot be covered by imports, and the moths arrive on spring winds from overwintering areas such as Hanoi and Nanning with Taiwan on the route. Gold medal, no awards or nominations. Same crop, same island, same pest-pressure problem as ReLEAF, approached from entomology rather than abiotic stress — the most obvious untapped adjacency in the cohort.","chips":["Gold","no awards","rice","crop protection","Chiayi"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Chiayi · id 6408 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Taichung · id 6062 — not on the briefed list","title":"WIST — ultrasound-reporting probiotic","body":"Washington International School, Taichung: an engineered E. coli that answers two chemical clues at once, lactate and nitrate, and reports the AND condition by filling with gas vesicles and becoming visible to ultrasound, as a swallowable early screen for colorectal cancer. The acoustic-reporter approach is the same gas-vesicle technology Heidelberg built its collegiate Top 10 project on this year, which makes it an ambitious choice for a high-school team. It carries both a Model and a Software page and declares every figure on the home page a diagram of method rather than acquired data. Gold medal, no awards; it attended the NYCU Meet-Up and appears on NCKU-Tainan's collaboration list.","chips":["Gold","no awards","gas vesicles","ultrasound","AND gate"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taichung · id 6062 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Taipei · id 6200 — not on the briefed list","title":"AEI Prep-Taiwan — SynPETic","body":"Engineered E. coli making PETase and MHETase side by side on one scaffold — a 'PETosome' — to depolymerise PET in water at 37 °C with no extruder and no metal catalyst, framed around the roughly 2,500 kg of plastic waste the ISS generates a year and the up-to-US$20,000 cost of lifting a kilogram to orbit. One of only two commercially organised Taiwanese high-school programmes besides GEMS and Labi, and it carries Model, Software and Hardware pages. Silver medal, no awards or nominations. The Space village framing makes it the nearest cohort neighbour to GEMS's own village placement.","chips":["Silver","no awards","PETase","Space village","Taipei"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taipei · id 6200 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Taipei · id 6423 — not on the briefed list","title":"VIS — Cadture","body":"VIS@betterworld Lab, testing whether engineered metallothioneins can capture cadmium from industrial wastewater, with a modelling page on cadmium removal. The notable feature is epistemic honesty of the kind GEMS also practises: the home page states that current work measures bacterial growth and GFP response and that direct cadmium removal remains to be tested, rather than implying a result it does not have. Silver medal, no awards or nominations. It attended the NYCU Meet-Up and is on NCKU-Tainan's collaboration list, so it is inside the island network that the Taipei commercial programmes are outside.","chips":["Silver","no awards","metallothionein","cadmium","honest scoping"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taipei · id 6423 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Zhubei · id 6156 — not on the briefed list","title":"HIA-Taiwan — Aiy-U-Ready","body":"Hsinchu International Academy in Zhubei, working on aiyu, Ficus pumila var. awkeotsang, a fig endemic to Taiwan that yields hundreds of tonnes a year and is almost unknown outside it. The project is built around that asymmetry — a locally owned crop nobody else is characterising — which is precisely the 'own a dataset nobody else has' logic the industry trend research identifies as a small institution's only durable asset. Silver medal, no awards or nominations, with a Dry Lab model page. It attended the NYCU Meet-Up and is on NCKU-Tainan's collaboration list.","chips":["Silver","no awards","aiyu","endemic crop","Hsinchu County"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Zhubei · id 6156 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · New Taipei · id 6103 — not on the briefed list","title":"KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei — Herculyeast","body":"Kang Chiao International School's Xiugang campus, running a yeast project with both Model and Software pages under its Dry Lab, plus Entrepreneurship, Inclusivity and Sustainability sections. Silver medal, no awards or nominations. Its sibling campus at Linkou entered separately as Taipei-TWN and was recorded as not eligible, so the Kang Chiao group fielded two high-school entries in 2026 and converted neither — and Labi-Taiwan, the iGEMers Prize winner, is the same Linkou programme's earlier lineage under a new organiser.","chips":["Silver","no awards","yeast","New Taipei","Kang Chiao"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · New Taipei · id 6103 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"Did not compete · ids 6142, 6543 — not on the briefed list","title":"Taipei-TWN and Oros Biotech","body":"Two Taiwanese registrations that never reached the competition floor and so are missing from every results table. Taipei-TWN (Kang Chiao International School, Linkou campus, high school, Taipei) carries the status 'not eligible' with no medal and no wiki content. Oros Biotech of Taichung entered the venture-foundry track rather than the competition, has no section, no medal and a 404 wiki — meaning Taiwan's only 2026 entry into iGEM's startup pathway left no public record. Both matter for the denominator: fifteen Taiwanese registrations, thirteen competing teams, and an entrepreneurship route the island used once and did not document.","chips":["Not eligible","venture foundry","no wiki","Taipei","Taichung"],"kicker_zh":"未參賽 · ids 6142, 6543 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"Regional comparison","title":"Taiwan against China, Hong Kong, Japan, Korea and Singapore","body":"On accepted competing teams: China 176, Hong Kong 16, Taiwan 13, Japan 7, Korea 6, Singapore 4. On outright wins Taiwan placed second in the region with six, behind China's 24 and ahead of Hong Kong's three, with Japan, Korea and Singapore returning none at all — so Taiwan was the only territory outside China to win more than once. On altitude the ranking inverts: China took five Top 10 places and a Grand Prize first runner-up, Hong Kong three Top 10 places and the high-school Grand Prize first runner-up through HongKong-JSS, Singapore one through NUS-Singapore, and Taiwan one through GEMS-Taiwan, with no Taiwanese Grand Prize placing at any tier. In kind the regions differ sharply: China dominates the parts awards and the Registry layer, Hong Kong spreads thirteen nominations across parts, model, software, hardware, education, presentation and wiki, Japan accumulates nominations without converting any, and Taiwan concentrates in hardware, measurement and human practices while taking zero parts and zero software nominations.","chips":["TWN 13 teams","6 wins","1 Top 10","0 parts","0 software","HKG 3 Top 10"],"kicker_zh":"區域比較"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Tier","2026 result","Strength"],"rows":[["GEMS-Taiwan (6072)","High School","Gold; Top 10; wins in Measurement, Hardware, Integrated HP; nominees Presentation, Wiki, Village Project","Provenance discipline, pre-registration, four built devices"],["Labi-Taiwan (6511)","High School","Gold; iGEMers Prize winner; Best Measurement nominee","Sequencing-to-target evidence integration; portable electrochemical readout"],["Mingdao (6105)","High School","Gold; Best Model nominee","Enzyme-kinetic and coupled-ODE modelling; integrated single-frame fermentor"],["WIST (6062)","High School","Gold; no awards","Gas-vesicle ultrasound reporting; two-input AND logic"],["AEI Prep-Taiwan (6200)","High School","Silver; no awards","Scaffolded dual-enzyme PET depolymerisation; Space village framing"],["VIS (6423)","High School","Silver; no awards","Metallothionein cadmium capture; honest scoping of untested claims"],["HIA-Taiwan (6156)","High School","Silver; no awards","Taiwan-endemic aiyu crop nobody else is characterising"],["KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei (6103)","High School","Silver; no awards","Yeast chassis with both model and software pages"],["NYCU-Taiwan (6306)","Undergrad","Silver; Best Project Promotion Video winner","Communication, convening; four-layer Cas12a model stack and probe-design software"],["NCKU-Tainan (6379)","Undergrad","Gold; Best Infectious Diseases Project winner; Best Hardware nominee","Inferential statistics with held-out prediction; US$54-161 fluorescence reader"],["NTHU Taiwan (6416)","Undergrad","Gold; no awards","Four models that each reversed or changed a build decision; open-source MBBR"],["CCU-Taiwan (6408)","Undergrad","Gold; no awards","Rice leafroller entomology and rice-trade economics"],["NTHU (6460)","Overgrad","Gold; Best Food & Nutrition Project nominee","Deepest computation in the cohort: receptor prediction, odour decoding, lock-in optics"],["Taipei-TWN (6142)","High School","Not eligible; no medal","No public record"],["Oros Biotech (6543)","Venture foundry","No section, no medal, 404 wiki","Taiwan's only 2026 entry to iGEM's startup pathway"]]},"partners":[{"name":"NTHU Taiwan (National Tsing Hua University, Hsinchu) — team 6416","why":"The closest technical match to GEMS on the island and the one GEMS has no relationship with. Same chassis (engineered Bacillus subtilis), same commitment to open-source reactor hardware (CathaBench, a three-tank MBBR on ESP32 with an offline dashboard), and a modelling culture that demonstrably changed the build rather than decorating it — it dropped dissolved oxygen from a screen on a predicted 6% separation, reversed an enzyme-engineering plan when formaldehyde was projected to five times chassis tolerance, and reversed a nozzle geometry after first-principles hydraulics. It also already holds the ITRI and industry relationships GEMS would otherwise have to build from nothing. It won gold and nothing else, so it needs legibility as much as GEMS needs rigour.","firstProject":"A joint Bacillus subtilis measurement standard. Co-characterise the CcaSR green-light transfer function and a suspension-versus-biofilm growth model across both teams' reactors in absolute fluorescein-calibrated units, then release it as a SubtiToolKit-compatible part collection with full transfer curves and a shared SBOL3 record. This closes GEMS's single largest hole — a control architecture resting on a Hill curve it never measured — and gives NTHU Taiwan the Registry-visible artefact its modelling earned and did not get."},{"name":"NCKU-Tainan (National Cheng Kung University, Tainan) — team 6379","why":"The only Taiwanese collegiate team to win a technical-domain award in 2026, and the holder of the exact competence GEMS lacks: mixed models with plate as a random intercept, geometric-mean-ratio effect sizes with 95% intervals, and a held-out treatment used as a genuine prediction test. It is also an instrumentation peer — CAPTURE-Screen reads GFP at US$54-161 against US$3,500 for the open-source plate reader it replaces, and LasReader wraps 4PL calibration with confidence intervals around any reader's output. It is the de facto mentoring spine of Taiwanese iGEM, having run a session for Mingdao with three of its own members as Mingdao alumni, so a GEMS link here also buys entry to the network GEMS skipped.","firstProject":"A cross-instrument calibration round-robin. Run GEMS's in-line photometer, NCKU's CAPTURE-Screen and a benchtop plate reader against the same fluorescein and silica standards and the same sfGFP culture series, analyse everything through LasReader so the analysis path is identical, and publish a Taiwan measurement note reporting agreement, disagreement and the limits of each instrument's linear range. It is a Best Measurement-grade artefact for both teams and it imports NCKU's statistics into GEMS's practice by doing rather than by telling."},{"name":"CCU-Taiwan (National Chung Cheng University, Chiayi) — team 6408","why":"Working the same crop, the same island and the same problem from the other side: rice under pest pressure rather than rice under abiotic stress. Its framing already matches GEMS's economic argument — that only about 12% of world rice crosses a border, so an Asian yield loss cannot be imported away — and it brings entomology and migration data (spring leafroller flights north from Hanoi and Nanning with Taiwan on the route) that GEMS's stress index does not contain. Gold medal, no awards, no obvious outlet for the work. Geographically it sits between Tainan and Taichung, inside the rice belt both projects target.","firstProject":"A shared Taiwan rice-stress dataset with a published benchmark. Extend GEMS's fitted stress index — 25 years of county rice yields against ERA5 daily reanalysis, scored across 32,767 candidate term combinations — with CCU's leafroller pressure and arrival data, release it as a versioned, licensed dataset with a defined forecasting benchmark task and a public leaderboard, and have both teams state a trigger rule against it in advance. One hectare, two trigger rules, one open benchmark that other teams can beat."},{"name":"NTHU (National Tsing Hua University, Hsinchu, overgrad AeroSense group) — team 6460","why":"The deepest computational work in the Taiwanese cohort and the natural counterpart to GEMS's protein-design pipeline. It runs receptor-response prediction with measured infrared and quantum-vibration features, an OpenPOM comparison, mutation-robustness and cross-species transfer tests, and molecular-dynamics pocket-entry studies — and it says openly that its decoder was evaluated on external metal-oxide sensor datasets rather than on its own cells. GEMS has the opposite problem: a GRAFT design workflow with docking, all-atom MD and a pre-set AlphaFold confidence gate, and almost no measured validation of what it designs. Each team is the other's missing half.","firstProject":"A design-to-measurement validation loop. GEMS proposes a small, pre-registered panel of receptor or binder variants through GRAFT with the confidence gate and acceptance criteria fixed in writing beforehand; NTHU expresses and measures them on its HEK293/GCaMP6f assay and four-channel lock-in reader; both publish the hit rate including every failure, with the predictions timestamped before the measurements. The deliverable is a hit-rate number on a named pipeline, which is the one thing neither team can currently produce alone."},{"name":"Labi-Taiwan (Labi Education, Taoyuan) — team 6511","why":"The only other Taiwanese high-school programme with a genuine computational stack, and GEMS's structural twin: both are Taipei-area programmes run by commercial organisers, both are absent from NYCU's and NCKU's collaboration lists, and between them they hold four of Taiwan's six 2026 wins. Their skills barely overlap — Labi runs sequencing-to-target evidence integration (2,656 miRNAs narrowed to miR-124-3p through differential expression, miRNA-mRNA networks, GSEA and WGCNA), ML-prioritised nucleic-acid probe design and electrochemical readout, where GEMS runs sensor metrology, reactor control and provenance auditing. Labi's iGEMers Prize also proves it can carry a room, which is the reputational asset a teaching programme needs.","firstProject":"A two-module Taiwan high-school dry-lab school, co-taught and open to any Taiwanese team. GEMS teaches provenance ledgers, assumption registers, pre-registration with written pass criteria and instrument cross-calibration; Labi teaches target selection from public sequencing cohorts, probe design and electrochemical quantification. Every participating team leaves with one pre-registered prediction, scored publicly after their next experiment. Teaching is also how GEMS joins the island network it currently sits outside."},{"name":"NYCU-Taiwan (National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University, Hsinchu) — team 6306","why":"The island's convening institution and its best communicators. It hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up at its Bo-Ai campus on 27 July for 53 students and advisors from five teams, built a dedicated Taiwan iGEMers exchange website as the public record, and won Best Project Promotion Video. It also sits in Hsinchu alongside both NTHU teams, TBMC's new GMP facility and ITRI, which makes it the right physical venue for anything recurring. What its meet-up lacked was technical content: the roundtables covered team cohesion, leadership and Jamboree preparation, not modelling or measurement.","firstProject":"Co-host the 2027 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up with a dry-lab track, and stand up a permanent Taiwan iGEM dry-lab repository behind it. NYCU supplies the venue, the convening and the website; GEMS supplies a half-day curriculum on modelling, calibration and reproducibility plus the repository's founding contents — shared calibration protocols, fluorescein standards, model code, SBOL3 construct records and a template pre-registration form. The test of success is that a 2027 team other than GEMS publishes a calibrated measurement using it."}],"method":"The tally is built from research/results2026.json (captured from competition.igem.org/results/2026 on 19 November 2026) cross-checked team by team against iGEM's own public API — api.igem.org/v1/teams?year=2026 for the full 463-team roster with countries, cities, sections and acceptance status, and api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>/awards for each team's medals, nominations and wins — which is how nine Taiwanese registrations absent from the results table were found, including NTHU Taiwan (6416), CCU-Taiwan (6408), WIST (6062) and AEI Prep-Taiwan (6200). Project detail comes from the teams' own 2026 wikis, read directly where server-rendered and through a browser for the client-rendered single-page sites (Labi-Taiwan, CCU-Taiwan), plus the existing researched file at research/teams/6072.json for GEMS-Taiwan and research/trends/industry.json for the TBMC, DayOne and Israel Innovation Authority figures. Two Taiwanese registrations could not be verified beyond their API records: Taipei-TWN (6142) is marked not eligible and has no wiki content, and Oros Biotech (6543) returns a 404 wiki, so nothing is claimed about either project; KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei's project could only be identified by name and navigation structure because its wiki ships a largely unmodified template, and Mingdao's medal-level claims rest on the API rather than on a wiki statement.","kicker_zh":"原創分析"},{"id":"technique-census","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What 2026's best teams actually reached for","title_zh":"2026 年最強的團隊，實際上用了什麼","lede":"A census of the computational tools named across every team file in this report — and the one habit that separates the podium from everybody else.","lede_zh":"對本報告所有團隊檔案中提及的運算工具所做的普查——以及把頒獎台和其他人分開的那一個習慣。","body":"Across the team files gathered here, **AlphaFold is still the default**: it is named by roughly a third of teams, more than any other modelling tool, and more than twice as often as the open successors. Boltz appears in a handful of files, ESMFold in a handful more, RFdiffusion and ProteinMPNN in fewer still. The academic literature has already moved past this — open models now match or beat the gated flagship — but iGEM has not caught up. That lag is an opportunity: a team that works fluently with the current open stack is doing something most of the competition is not.\n\nThe second pattern is that **the dedicated systems-biology tools have quietly lost**. COPASI, once the standard way an iGEM team built a kinetic model, appears in one file. Tellurium appears in one. MATLAB holds on in four. Everything else is Python — named by more teams than any other single item in the census, usually SciPy integrating an ODE system written by hand. Teaching COPASI as the entry point to modelling now teaches a tool the field has left behind.\n\nThe third pattern is the surprise. **Techno-economic analysis — costing the thing, modelling unit economics — is done by more high-school teams than undergraduate teams**, in absolute numbers as well as proportionally. High-school teams are being pushed hard on implementation and business thinking, and they are delivering it. Meanwhile GROMACS, full molecular dynamics, appears exclusively in undergraduate files and never once in a high-school file. The two tiers are not weaker and stronger versions of each other; they are differently shaped.\n\n**Then the finding that matters.** We checked which teams do both halves of modelling properly: fit the model to their own measured data (parameter estimation, regression, R², RMSE, confidence intervals, error bars) *and* validate it against something held back (held-out data, cross-validation, a separate experimental test). Only 14 of 54 teams do both.\n\nOf those 14, **10 are Top 10 teams — 71%**. Of the 42 that do not close that loop, 17 are Top 10 — **40%**. Every one of the four who closed the loop without reaching a Top 10 won a major special prize anyway: XJTLU-China and Jilin-China in Best Model, NJU-China took Best Software & AI Project, Vilnius-Lithuania was nominated in three categories.\n\nThis is the single most actionable number in the report. Not which model you use — whether you close the loop between the model and your own data. It is also, conveniently, the cheapest capability to build: it needs no GPU, no licence and no collaboration. It needs a student who knows what a residual is.","body_zh":"在本報告蒐集的團隊檔案中，**AlphaFold 仍然是預設選項**：約三分之一的團隊提到它，比任何其他建模工具都多，也超過開源後繼者的兩倍以上。Boltz 出現在少數幾份檔案，ESMFold 再多一點，RFdiffusion 與 ProteinMPNN 更少。學術文獻早已走過這一步——開源模型現已可匹敵甚至超越封閉的旗艦模型——但 iGEM 還沒跟上。這個時間差就是機會：能熟練運用當前開源工具鏈的團隊，正在做大多數競爭者沒做的事。\n\n第二個型態是，**專用的系統生物學工具已悄悄落敗**。COPASI 曾經是 iGEM 團隊建立動力學模型的標準做法，如今只出現在一份檔案中。Tellurium 一份。MATLAB 勉強守住四份。其餘全是 Python——在整份普查中被提及的團隊數多於任何單一項目，通常是用 SciPy 積分一組手寫的 ODE 系統。現在把 COPASI 當作建模的入門，等於是在教一個領域已經放下的工具。\n\n第三個型態令人意外。**做技術經濟分析——計算成本、建立單位經濟模型——的高中隊伍比大學部隊伍還多**，絕對數與比例皆然。高中組被大力要求落實應用與商業思考，而他們做到了。相對地，完整的分子動力學（GROMACS）只出現在大學部的檔案中，高中組一次也沒有。這兩個層級不是同一件事的強弱版本，它們的形狀本來就不同。\n\n**接著是真正重要的發現。** 我們檢查了哪些團隊把建模的兩半都做完：以自己量到的資料擬合模型（參數估計、回歸、R²、RMSE、信賴區間、誤差棒），*並且*用保留的資料驗證它（held-out 資料、交叉驗證、獨立的實驗測試）。54 支團隊中只有 14 支兩者皆備。\n\n這 14 支裡，**有 10 支是 Top 10 團隊——71%**。而在沒有閉合這個迴圈的 42 支中，只有 17 支進入 Top 10——**40%**。閉合了迴圈卻未進 Top 10 的那四支，無一例外都拿下了重要特別獎：XJTLU-China 與 Jilin-China 在最佳模型，NJU-China 拿下最佳軟體與 AI 專案，Vilnius-Lithuania 則獲三項提名。\n\n這是整份報告中最可執行的一個數字。重點不是你用哪個模型，而是你有沒有把模型與自己的資料之間的迴圈閉合起來。而且它恰好也是最便宜的能力：不需要 GPU、不需要授權、不需要合作對象。它需要的是一位知道什麼叫殘差的學生。","cards":[{"kicker":"The headline number","title":"71% versus 40%","title_zh":"71% 對 40%","body":"Teams that both fit their model to their own data and validated it against something held back reached a Top 10 at 71%. Teams that did not reached it at 40%. Note the sample is already decorated — every team here is a Top 10 or special-prize team — so this is loop-closure separating winners from other winners, not from the general field.","body_zh":"既以自身資料擬合模型、又用保留資料加以驗證的團隊，進入 Top 10 的比例是 71%；沒有這麼做的則是 40%。請注意樣本本身已經過篩選——這裡每一支團隊都是 Top 10 或特別獎隊伍——因此這是「閉合迴圈」把贏家從其他贏家中分出來，而不是從一般參賽者中分出來。","chips":["14 of 54 closed the loop","10 of those 14 made Top 10"],"kicker_zh":"關鍵數字"},{"kicker":"Still the default","title":"AlphaFold has not been displaced inside iGEM","title_zh":"在 iGEM 裡，AlphaFold 還沒被取代","body":"Roughly a third of teams name AlphaFold, more than twice the rate of Boltz, ESMFold, RFdiffusion or ProteinMPNN. The research literature moved to the open stack over the past year; the competition has not. The teams already working in Boltz and the MPNN family — Lambert-GA, Heidelberg, GU Frankfurt, DTU-Denmark, Princeton — are visibly ahead of the curve rather than merely current.","body_zh":"約三分之一的團隊提到 AlphaFold，是 Boltz、ESMFold、RFdiffusion 或 ProteinMPNN 的兩倍以上。研究文獻在過去一年已轉向開源工具鏈，競賽卻還沒。已經在用 Boltz 與 MPNN 家族的隊伍——Lambert-GA、Heidelberg、GU Frankfurt、DTU-Denmark、Princeton——明顯走在前面，而不只是跟上。","chips":["AlphaFold ×19","Boltz ×7","ProteinMPNN ×7","RFdiffusion ×3"],"kicker_zh":"仍是預設選項"},{"kicker":"A tool generation ended","title":"Python ate the modelling stack","title_zh":"Python 吃掉了整個建模工具鏈","body":"COPASI appears once. Tellurium once. MATLAB four times. Python appears in more team files than any other item in the census, usually SciPy integrating a hand-written ODE system, with scikit-learn behind it for anything statistical. For a programme deciding what to teach, this settles the question: teach Python and the numerical stack, and treat SBML-based tools as an interchange format rather than a starting point.","body_zh":"COPASI 出現一次，Tellurium 一次，MATLAB 四次。Python 出現在比普查中任何其他項目都多的團隊檔案裡，通常是用 SciPy 積分手寫的 ODE 系統，統計部分則交給 scikit-learn。對一個正在決定要教什麼的課程而言，這已經定案：教 Python 與數值運算工具鏈，把以 SBML 為基礎的工具當作交換格式，而不是起點。","chips":["Python ×31","scikit-learn ×8","COPASI ×1","Tellurium ×1"],"kicker_zh":"一個工具世代的終結"},{"kicker":"The inversion","title":"High-school teams cost their projects; undergraduates often don't","title_zh":"高中隊伍會算成本，大學部常常不算","body":"Techno-economic analysis appears in more high-school files than undergraduate ones, both in absolute count and as a share of the tier. Full molecular dynamics runs the other way and is exclusively undergraduate. The tiers are differently shaped rather than simply further apart, and a high-school programme that assumes it must catch up on everything is aiming at the wrong gap.","body_zh":"技術經濟分析在高中組檔案中出現的次數，無論絕對數或組內占比都高於大學部；完整的分子動力學則完全相反，只出現在大學部。兩個層級的形狀不同，而不只是距離遠近的差別。一個假定自己必須在所有面向上追趕的高中課程，瞄錯了缺口。","chips":["Techno-economic: 7 HS vs 5 UG","GROMACS: 6 UG, 0 HS"],"kicker_zh":"反轉"},{"kicker":"A weaker result, reported anyway","title":"Publishing your failures: real, but a smaller effect than it looks","title_zh":"公開失敗：效果是真的，但沒有看起來那麼大","body":"Several analysts noticed the same thing independently — Toronto, WageningenUR and UZurich each put a prominent negative or failed result on the wiki, and two of them won the award in that exact category. We tested it across every file. Teams that openly report failure reach a Top 10 at 54%, against 41% for those that do not. That is a real gap, but it is far smaller than the loop-closure gap, and the measurement is partly circular: it detects how candid *our own summary* of a team was, not reliably how candid the team was. Treat it as a reason to publish the negative result, not as proof it wins prizes.","body_zh":"好幾位分析員各自獨立注意到同一件事——Toronto、WageningenUR 與 UZurich 都在 wiki 上顯著地放上了一個負面或失敗的結果，而其中兩隊正是在對應的獎項類別中獲獎。我們對所有檔案做了檢驗：公開報告失敗的團隊進入 Top 10 的比例是 54%，沒有這麼做的則是 41%。差距是真的，但遠小於「閉合迴圈」的差距，而且這個量測帶有循環性：它偵測到的是*我們自己的摘要*有多坦白，而未必能可靠反映團隊有多坦白。請把它當作「應該公開負面結果」的理由，而不是「這樣就會得獎」的證明。","chips":["54% vs 41%","measurement is confounded"],"kicker_zh":"較弱的結果，照樣報告"},{"kicker":"What this means for GEMS","title":"The cheapest capability is the one that correlates with winning","title_zh":"最便宜的能力，正好就是和得獎相關的那一個","body":"Closing the model-data loop needs no GPU, no licence, no partner lab and no new chassis. It needs a student who can fit a curve, report an uncertainty and hold data back for a test. That is a term's teaching, and on this evidence it moves the result more than any tool choice. It is Phase 2 of the roadmap for exactly this reason.","body_zh":"閉合模型與資料之間的迴圈，不需要 GPU、不需要授權、不需要合作實驗室、也不需要新的底盤。它需要的是一位會擬合曲線、會報告不確定度、並且懂得保留資料做測試的學生。那是一個學期的教學量，而根據這些證據，它對結果的影響大於任何工具選擇。這正是它成為路線圖階段二的原因。","chips":["No GPU required","One term of teaching"],"kicker_zh":"這對 GEMS 的意義"}],"method":"Counts come from pattern-matching the `dry` and `good` fields of every team file in this report, not from reading the wikis a second time, so a technique a team used but did not write up is invisible here. The sample is decorated teams only — every file is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee — so the baselines are not the whole competition. The loop-closure test looks for explicit language about fitting, uncertainty and validation; a team that did the work but described it loosely will be undercounted. Read the numbers as a ranking, not a measurement.","method_zh":"計數方式是對本報告每一份團隊檔案的 `dry` 與 `good` 欄位做樣式比對，而非重新閱讀 wiki，因此團隊做了卻沒寫下來的技術在這裡是看不見的。樣本僅限獲獎隊伍——每一份檔案都是 Top 10 或特別獎得主／入圍者——所以基準值並不代表整個競賽。迴圈閉合的判準是尋找明確描述擬合、不確定度與驗證的文字；做了卻寫得含糊的團隊會被低估。請把這些數字當成排序，而不是量測。","kicker_zh":"原創分析"},{"id":"wiki-craft","tab":"teams","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What the Best Wiki winners did differently","title_zh":"最佳 Wiki 得獎隊伍做了哪些不一樣的事","lede":"The four 2026 Best Wiki winners did not win on visual polish or page weight; they won by building an executive layer that tells a judge where the evidence is, and then by being unusually specific and unusually honest underneath it.","lede_zh":"2026 年四組最佳 Wiki 得獎隊伍並不是靠視覺精緻度或頁面重量取勝；他們靠的是建立一層明確的摘要層，直接告訴評審證據在哪裡，然後在這層底下做到異常具體、異常誠實。","body":"Three of the four winners ship pages whose text exists in the HTML before any JavaScript runs: **Heidelberg** writes static HTML by hand, **Uni-Padua-IT** prerenders SvelteKit, **Lambert-GA** builds with Astro. TU Delft is the exception, a Vite single-page app behind a 3.4 MB bundle, and it compensates deliberately with an `llms.txt` at the wiki root and a plain-Markdown mirror of every page at `/tu-delft/<page>.md`. Against that, the control group — Princeton, Cornell, LYON, UAlberta, UCNZ, Athens, GU Frankfurt and Eton-College-UK, all winners of serious 2026 science prizes — serves near-empty shells of 486 bytes to 15 kB, as little as seven characters of text without JS.\n\nThe real differentiator is an explicit executive layer. Uni-Padua-IT and Lambert-GA both ship a `/judging` page that walks medal criterion by criterion, summarises each in two or three sentences and deep-links the evidence — Padua pointing straight at its own negative results, Lambert stating in the summary that fifteen minibinder designs produced no confirmed hits before a second campaign of twenty produced one binder at roughly 604 nM. TU Delft reaches the same place with an illustrated module map on Results where hovering highlights a module and clicking jumps to it, over the same five modules that organise the project; Heidelberg puts three summary cards above the fold and gives every nav link a one-line subtitle, so \"Results\" reads \"Where data tells the story\".\n\nUnderneath, the winners are simply more specific. **Heidelberg**'s captions carry panel letters, 547 ng and 433 ng transfection masses, 18,000 × g, and an effect size quoted with its range — 5.6×, 4.3 to 6.4× depending on the haze setting — while Padua photographs the plate that grew nothing, numbers it as a figure, and explains why an earlier transformation failed. **TU Delft** built a content system rather than a set of pages: 1,604 reference tags over 735 unique DOIs, 724 glossary calls against 102 definitions, 307 auto-numbered figures, and one unvarying Background → Results → Discussion → Future Perspective spine. Its decision matrix tags every cell as Factual, Inferred, Estimated or Speculative, with a legend saying the tag records the strength of the evidence behind the cell rather than the judgement — epistemic honesty rendered as a UI component, and I saw nothing like it elsewhere.\n\nWhat did not decide it is as instructive. Page weight spans two orders of magnitude inside the winners' circle, from Lambert-GA's 78 kB homepage to TU Delft's 3.4 MB. None of Heidelberg, Uni-Padua, Lambert-GA, Stanford, UCAS-China or Toronto declares a `prefers-color-scheme` rule, and meaningful alt text ran at 27 to 48 per cent across the winners while HongKong-JSS, ProFuture-China and WageningenUR hit 90, 86 and 81 per cent and won nothing for it. The winners do all honour `prefers-reduced-motion` — thirteen blocks in Heidelberg's stylesheet, eleven in TU Delft's bundle — and Heidelberg goes further, sniffing for a software WebGL renderer and dropping to a lite mode automatically, with `?lite=0` and `?perf=1` for anyone who wants to look: the motion budget goes to figure interactions and graceful degradation, not to hero spectacle.","body_zh":"四組得獎隊伍中有三組，頁面文字在任何 JavaScript 執行之前就已經存在於 HTML 裡：**Heidelberg** 手寫靜態 HTML，**Uni-Padua-IT** 以 SvelteKit 預先渲染，**Lambert-GA** 用 Astro 建置。TU Delft 是例外，它是一個 3.4 MB bundle 的 Vite 單頁應用，而它刻意用 wiki 根目錄的 `llms.txt`，以及每一頁在 `/tu-delft/<page>.md` 的純 Markdown 鏡像來補償。相對地，對照組——Princeton、Cornell、LYON、UAlberta、UCNZ、Athens、GU Frankfurt 和 Eton-College-UK，全都是 2026 年重量級科學獎項的得主——送出的是 486 位元組到 15 kB 的近乎空殼，在沒有 JS 的情況下最少只有七個字元的文字。\n\n真正的分水嶺是一層明確的摘要層。Uni-Padua-IT 和 Lambert-GA 都提供 `/judging` 頁面，逐條走過每一項獎牌標準，每一項用兩三句話摘要，並深層連結到證據——Padua 直接指向自己的負面結果，Lambert 在摘要裡寫明十五個 minibinder 設計沒有產生任何確認的命中，第二輪二十個設計才做出一個親和力約 604 nM 的 binder。TU Delft 以另一種方式到達同一處：Results 頁上一張插圖式的模組地圖，滑鼠移過會凸顯某個模組，點擊則跳到該模組，涵蓋的正是組織整個專案的那五個模組；Heidelberg 把三張摘要卡放在首屏之上，並給每個導覽連結一行副標，於是「Results」讀起來是「Where data tells the story」。\n\n再往下看，得獎隊伍就只是更具體。**Heidelberg** 的圖說帶有分圖編號、547 ng 與 433 ng 的轉染量、18,000 × g，以及附上範圍的效應量——5.6 倍，依 haze 設定落在 4.3 到 6.4 倍之間——而 Padua 把什麼都沒長出來的培養盤拍下來、編上圖號，並解釋早先一次轉形為何失敗。**TU Delft** 建的是一套內容系統，而不是一疊頁面：1,604 個引用標記對應 735 個不重複的 DOI、724 次詞彙表呼叫對應 102 條定義、307 張自動編號的圖，以及一條從不變動的 Background → Results → Discussion → Future Perspective 骨幹。它的決策矩陣為每一格標上 Factual、Inferred、Estimated 或 Speculative，圖例並說明這個標記記錄的是該格背後證據的強度，而不是判斷本身——把知識論上的誠實做成一個介面元件，這種作法我在別處沒有看到。\n\n沒有決定勝負的因素同樣值得一看。得獎圈內的頁面重量橫跨兩個數量級，從 Lambert-GA 78 kB 的首頁到 TU Delft 的 3.4 MB。Heidelberg、Uni-Padua、Lambert-GA、Stanford、UCAS-China 和 Toronto 都沒有宣告任何 `prefers-color-scheme` 規則；有意義的替代文字在得獎隊伍之間只有 27% 到 48%，而 HongKong-JSS、ProFuture-China 和 WageningenUR 分別達到 90%、86% 和 81%，卻沒有因此得到任何獎。得獎隊伍確實全都尊重 `prefers-reduced-motion`——Heidelberg 的樣式表裡有十三段，TU Delft 的 bundle 裡有十一段——而 Heidelberg 走得更遠，它會偵測軟體 WebGL 轉譯器並自動降為輕量模式，還留了 `?lite=0` 和 `?perf=1` 給想細看的人：動態效果的預算花在圖表互動和優雅降級上，而不是首頁的視覺奇觀。","cards":[{"kicker":"Information architecture","title":"Build a judging page and make it the front door","title_zh":"做一個 judging 頁面，並讓它成為正門","body":"Uni-Padua-IT and Lambert-GA each ship a `/judging` route that indexes every medal criterion and every award they apply for. Each entry is two or three sentences of plain summary followed by a deep link into the page that holds the evidence. Padua links directly to its own failed Design-Build-Test-Learn cycles under Silver; Lambert quotes the binding affinity and the two failed design campaigns in the Gold section. It costs one page and it converts a pile of required sections into a reading order.","body_zh":"Uni-Padua-IT 和 Lambert-GA 各自提供一個 `/judging` 路徑，索引每一條獎牌標準和每一個申請的獎項。每一則是兩三句樸素的摘要，後面接一個深層連結，直通存放證據的頁面。Padua 在銀牌項下直接連到自己失敗的 Design-Build-Test-Learn 循環；Lambert 在金牌段落引用結合親和力和兩次失敗的設計輪次。代價是一頁，換來的是把一堆規定章節轉成一條閱讀動線。","chips":["Uni-Padua-IT","Lambert-GA","2 clicks to evidence","One page"],"kicker_zh":"資訊架構"},{"kicker":"Data presentation","title":"Label the provenance of every number you did not measure","title_zh":"為每一個不是你量出來的數字標註來源","body":"TU Delft's entrepreneurship page scores four candidate applications against eleven weighted parameters. Every single cell carries a bracketed tag — [F]actual, [I]nferred, [E]stimated or [S]peculative — and the legend states that the tag records how strong the evidence behind the cell is, not the score, because every score is a judgement applied to sourced facts. The weights sum to 100 per cent and the weighted total is given to two decimals. It is the single most copyable device I found in 2026.","body_zh":"TU Delft 的創業頁面用十一個加權參數為四個候選應用評分。每一格都帶一個方括號標記——[F]actual、[I]nferred、[E]stimated 或 [S]peculative——圖例說明這個標記記錄的是該格背後證據有多強，而不是分數本身，因為每個分數都是對有來源的事實所做的判斷。權重加總為 100%，加權總分給到小數第二位。這是我在 2026 年找到最值得照抄的一項設計。","chips":["TU Delft","F / I / E / S","Weighted matrix","Shows its working"],"kicker_zh":"資料呈現"},{"kicker":"Human practices","title":"Date every pivot and name who caused it","title_zh":"為每一次轉向標上日期，並指名是誰造成的","body":"Lambert-GA applies one named framework, H.I.V.E. — Hear, Inquire, Validate, Evolve — identically to every stakeholder, then closes with a Project Pivots timeline. Five entries, each with a date, the named expert whose feedback caused it, and a literal before-and-after: nanobody changed to minibinder, P-domain in general changed to specific hotspots. The caption says every change shown came directly from stakeholder feedback rather than internal decisions. It makes integration auditable instead of asserted.","body_zh":"Lambert-GA 對每一位利害關係人都套用同一個具名框架 H.I.V.E.——Hear、Inquire、Validate、Evolve——最後以一條 Project Pivots 時間軸收尾。五則記錄，每一則都有日期、意見造成這次轉向的具名專家，以及字面上的前後對照：nanobody 改成 minibinder，整個 P-domain 改成特定的熱點。圖說寫明所列的每一項改變都直接來自利害關係人的意見，而不是團隊內部的決定。這讓整合變成可查核的，而不是宣稱的。","chips":["Lambert-GA","H.I.V.E.","Dated timeline","Before → after"],"kicker_zh":"人類實踐"},{"kicker":"Technical build","title":"Mirror the wiki as plain Markdown","title_zh":"把 wiki 鏡像成純 Markdown","body":"TU Delft's wiki is a Vite single-page app and the heaviest I measured, yet it publishes an `llms.txt` at the wiki root listing twelve pages, each mirrored as plain Markdown at `/tu-delft/<page>.md`. That gives a JS-free fallback, a machine-readable corpus, and a diffable source of truth for the content, all from one build step. If you insist on a client-rendered framework, this is the tax you should pay for it.","body_zh":"TU Delft 的 wiki 是 Vite 單頁應用，也是我量過最重的一個，但它在 wiki 根目錄發布 `llms.txt`，列出十二個頁面，每一頁都在 `/tu-delft/<page>.md` 鏡像成純 Markdown。這一個建置步驟同時換來不需要 JS 的替代方案、一份機器可讀的語料，以及一份可以做 diff 的內容真實來源。如果你堅持要用客戶端渲染的框架，這就是你該付的稅。","chips":["TU Delft","llms.txt","/page.md","JS-free fallback"],"kicker_zh":"技術實作"},{"kicker":"Figures","title":"Write captions that stand alone, and number the negative control","title_zh":"寫能獨立成立的圖說，並為陰性對照編上圖號","body":"Heidelberg's captions carry panel letters, exact reagent masses, exact centrifugation and pressure conditions, and effect sizes quoted with a range across settings — a reader can take the figure out of the page and still understand it. Uni-Padua-IT goes one better on controls: the plate that grew nothing gets its own numbered figure with the full condition in the caption, sitting beside the plate that grew two colonies. Showing the control is cheap and it is the fastest way to look like you know what you are doing.","body_zh":"Heidelberg 的圖說帶有分圖編號、確切的試劑用量、確切的離心與壓力條件，以及跨設定給出範圍的效應量——讀者把圖從頁面裡拿出來也看得懂。Uni-Padua-IT 在對照組上更進一步：什麼都沒長出來的培養盤有自己的圖號，圖說裡寫出完整條件，就放在長出兩個菌落的培養盤旁邊。把對照組放出來很便宜，而且這是讓人看起來知道自己在做什麼的最快方法。","chips":["Heidelberg","Uni-Padua-IT","Units + n + conditions","Show the control"],"kicker_zh":"圖表"},{"kicker":"Build discipline","title":"Keep content out of components","title_zh":"別把內容寫進元件裡","body":"Stanford University — Grand Prize winner and a Best Wiki nominee, though not a winner — stores each page as a single hand-written JavaScript object with a documented block grammar of p, sh, gal, list, table, steps, math and quotes, plus a per-page accent colour and icon. TU Delft does the equivalent in MDX with a fixed component vocabulary. Either way the layout is written once and the copy is written by people who are not touching layout, which is why neither wiki drifts between pages.","body_zh":"Stanford University——總冠軍得主，也是最佳 Wiki 入圍者，但沒有得獎——把每一頁存成一個手寫的 JavaScript 物件，配上一套文件化的區塊語法：p、sh、gal、list、table、steps、math 和 quotes，再加上每頁自己的強調色與圖示。TU Delft 則用 MDX 搭配固定的元件詞彙做到同一件事。不論哪一種，版面只寫一次，文字由不碰版面的人來寫，這就是這兩個 wiki 不會在頁與頁之間走樣的原因。","chips":["Stanford University","TU Delft","One file per page","Block grammar"],"kicker_zh":"建置紀律"},{"kicker":"Craft","title":"Degrade on purpose, not by accident","title_zh":"刻意降級，而不是意外降級","body":"Heidelberg's wiki detects a software WebGL renderer on load and automatically switches to a lite mode, with `?lite=0` and `?lite=1` to force it either way and `?perf=1` to load a performance reporter. Its stylesheet carries thirteen `prefers-reduced-motion` blocks; TU Delft's bundle carries eleven. The winners treat a judge on a tired laptop as a real user. Nobody built a dark mode, and nobody needed one.","body_zh":"Heidelberg 的 wiki 在載入時偵測軟體 WebGL 轉譯器，並自動切換到輕量模式，另有 `?lite=0` 和 `?lite=1` 可以強制切換，`?perf=1` 則載入效能回報器。它的樣式表裡有十三段 `prefers-reduced-motion`；TU Delft 的 bundle 裡有十一段。得獎隊伍把用著一台老舊筆電的評審當成真實使用者。沒有人做深色模式，也沒有人需要。","chips":["Heidelberg","?lite=1","prefers-reduced-motion","Hardware sniffing"],"kicker_zh":"工藝"}],"table":{"head":["Wiki","Section","Framework / build","The one thing it does best"],"head_zh":["Wiki","組別","框架／建置","它做得最好的一件事"],"rows":[["Heidelberg","Undergrad — winner","Hand-written static HTML, Bootstrap plus a 77 kB token layer; ~1 MB of HTML, CSS and JS","Journal-grade figure captions, and an automatic lite mode for weak GPUs"],["Uni-Padua-IT","Undergrad — winner","SvelteKit, prerendered; 266 kB across 17 code-split files","A /judging page that links each medal criterion straight at the evidence, failures included"],["TU Delft","Overgrad — winner","Vite SPA, one 3.4 MB bundle, 16 flat routes; MDX content with a fixed component vocabulary","Per-cell evidence-provenance labels, plus every page mirrored as Markdown behind llms.txt"],["Lambert-GA","High School — winner","Astro, fully static; 78 kB of HTML, CSS and JS on the homepage","A dated pivot timeline that attributes each project change to a named stakeholder"],["Stanford University","Undergrad — nominee","Client-rendered template app; 15 hand-written content files with a documented block grammar","Content fully separated from layout, so nothing drifts between pages"],["UCAS-China","Undergrad — nominee","Static HTML, 18 pages including a /medal index","An odometer-style opening statistic that lands the problem in one screen"]],"rows_zh":[["Heidelberg","大學組——得獎","手寫靜態 HTML，Bootstrap 加一層 77 kB 的 token 層；HTML、CSS 與 JS 合計約 1 MB","期刊級的圖說，以及針對弱 GPU 的自動輕量模式"],["Uni-Padua-IT","大學組——得獎","SvelteKit，預先渲染；17 個程式碼分割檔案共 266 kB","/judging 頁面把每一條獎牌標準直接連到證據，失敗的部分也包含在內"],["TU Delft","研究生組——得獎","Vite 單頁應用，單一 3.4 MB bundle，16 條扁平路由；MDX 內容搭配固定的元件詞彙","逐格標註證據來源，並把每一頁鏡像成 Markdown 放在 llms.txt 後面"],["Lambert-GA","高中組——得獎","Astro，完全靜態；首頁的 HTML、CSS 與 JS 合計 78 kB","一條標了日期的轉向時間軸，把每次專案變更歸因到具名的利害關係人"],["Stanford University","大學組——入圍","客戶端渲染的樣板應用；15 個手寫內容檔，搭配文件化的區塊語法","內容與版面完全分離，所以頁與頁之間不會走樣"],["UCAS-China","大學組——入圍","靜態 HTML，18 個頁面，含一個 /medal 索引","里程表式的開場統計數字，一個畫面就把問題講清楚"]]},"checklist":["Ship HTML that already contains your words — prerender, or mirror every page as Markdown with an llms.txt, as TU Delft did.","Build a /judging page that answers each medal criterion in two or three sentences and deep-links the evidence.","State the controlling question on the first screen and repeat it in the same words on every summary layer.","Put a three-card or five-module summary above the detail on every long page, before any subsection.","Fix one spine for every results subsection — Background, Results, Discussion, Future Perspective — and never vary it.","Write captions that stand alone: panel letters, exact conditions, units, n, and the effect size with its range.","Photograph the negative control and give it a figure number of its own.","Name your failures with numbers, and name them in the executive layer rather than burying them.","Tag the provenance of every number you did not measure yourself — factual, inferred, estimated or speculative.","Keep content in one data file per page with a documented block grammar; let layout be written once.","Date every human-practices pivot, name the person whose feedback caused it, and show before and after.","Honour prefers-reduced-motion and spend the motion budget on figure interactions, not on the hero."],"checklist_zh":["送出已經包含你文字的 HTML——預先渲染，或像 TU Delft 那樣把每一頁鏡像成 Markdown 並配上 llms.txt。","做一個 /judging 頁面，用兩三句話回答每一條獎牌標準，並深層連結到證據。","在第一個畫面就寫出主導問題，並在每一層摘要用一模一樣的字重複它。","在每一個長頁面的細節之前，放上三張卡片或五個模組的摘要，排在任何子章節之前。","為每一個結果子章節固定同一條骨幹——Background、Results、Discussion、Future Perspective——而且絕不變動。","寫能獨立成立的圖說：分圖編號、確切條件、單位、n，以及附上範圍的效應量。","把陰性對照拍下來，並給它自己的圖號。","用數字說出你的失敗，而且要說在摘要層裡，不要埋起來。","為每一個不是你自己量出來的數字標註來源——事實、推論、估計或推測。","把內容放在每頁一個資料檔裡，搭配文件化的區塊語法；版面只寫一次。","為每一次人類實踐的轉向標上日期、指名是誰的意見造成的，並呈現前後對照。","尊重 prefers-reduced-motion，把動態效果的預算花在圖表互動上，而不是首頁主視覺。"],"antipatterns":["Dark mode and theme toggles. Not one of Heidelberg, Uni-Padua-IT, Lambert-GA, Stanford, UCAS-China or Toronto declares a prefers-color-scheme rule, and all of them placed well.","A late alt-text compliance sweep. The four winners ran 27 to 48 per cent meaningful alt text while HongKong-JSS (90 per cent), ProFuture-China (86) and WageningenUR (81) all beat them and none was a Best Wiki winner — it is a floor, not a differentiator, so do it early and cheaply.","Huge homepage media galleries. Toronto pulls 214 images and 252 .avif references on the homepage alone and ETH-Zurich serves a single 1.9 MB HTML page; neither won Best Wiki.","A client-rendered SPA with no text fallback. This is the default in the control group — Princeton, Cornell, LYON, UAlberta, UCNZ, Athens, GU Frankfurt and Eton-College-UK all serve near-empty shells despite winning major science prizes.","Per-page mascots, bespoke icon sets and per-page accent colours. Stanford invested in all three and placed as a nominee; none of the four winners has a mascot system.","Treating the mandatory section list as the information architecture. A deep-linked judging index does the same job in one page and reads as an argument rather than a form."],"antipatterns_zh":["深色模式與主題切換。Heidelberg、Uni-Padua-IT、Lambert-GA、Stanford、UCAS-China 和 Toronto 沒有一個宣告 prefers-color-scheme 規則，而他們的名次全都不錯。","最後才做一輪替代文字合規清查。四組得獎隊伍有意義的替代文字只有 27% 到 48%，而 HongKong-JSS（90%）、ProFuture-China（86%）和 WageningenUR（81%）都勝過他們，卻沒有一個是最佳 Wiki 得主——這是底線，不是差異點，所以早做、便宜做就好。","首頁放巨大的媒體圖庫。Toronto 光首頁就拉了 214 張圖和 252 個 .avif 參照，ETH-Zurich 送出單一 1.9 MB 的 HTML 頁面；兩者都沒有拿到最佳 Wiki。","客戶端渲染的單頁應用，而且沒有任何文字替代方案。這是對照組的預設做法——Princeton、Cornell、LYON、UAlberta、UCNZ、Athens、GU Frankfurt 和 Eton-College-UK 全都送出近乎空殼的頁面，儘管他們都拿下了重要的科學獎項。","每頁一隻吉祥物、客製圖示組和每頁不同的強調色。Stanford 三者都投資了，結果只是入圍；四組得獎隊伍沒有一個有吉祥物系統。","把規定的章節清單當成資訊架構。一個深層連結的 judging 索引用一頁就做到同一件事，而且讀起來像論證，不像表格。"],"method":"I rendered and read the four winners in full — Heidelberg, Uni-Padua-IT, TU Delft and Lambert-GA — by fetching their page HTML directly where it is server-rendered, by reading TU Delft's Markdown mirrors, and by loading the client-rendered pages in a browser; counts of references, figures, components, image formats, alt attributes and prefers-reduced-motion rules were taken from the shipped source. I sampled around thirty nominees and controls more shallowly, measuring framework, rendered text length, asset weight and alt-text coverage for all of them, and reading Stanford's and UCAS-China's content in detail as the closest nominees. I could not render several Vite single-page nominees deeply — Oxford, UCSC, NUS-Singapore, KAUST-KSA, Muenster-University, IISER-Kolkata and UOttawa among them — because a shared browser pane kept being navigated away mid-session, so they are excluded from the table and their design is not characterised here; I also did not measure real-world load time, mobile layout or screen-reader behaviour beyond the markup.","method_zh":"我完整渲染並讀過四組得獎隊伍——Heidelberg、Uni-Padua-IT、TU Delft 和 Lambert-GA：伺服器端渲染的部分直接抓取頁面 HTML，TU Delft 的部分讀它的 Markdown 鏡像，客戶端渲染的頁面則在瀏覽器中載入；引用、圖、元件、影像格式、alt 屬性和 prefers-reduced-motion 規則的數量，都取自實際送出的原始碼。我以較淺的方式抽樣約三十組入圍隊伍與對照隊伍，為全部這些隊伍量測框架、渲染後文字長度、資產重量和替代文字覆蓋率，並把 Stanford 與 UCAS-China 的內容當成最接近的入圍者細讀。有幾組 Vite 單頁應用的入圍隊伍我無法深入渲染——包括 Oxford、UCSC、NUS-Singapore、KAUST-KSA、Muenster-University、IISER-Kolkata 和 UOttawa——因為共用的瀏覽器面板在過程中一直被導向其他頁面，所以它們不列入表格，本文也不描述它們的設計；此外，除了標記語言本身之外，我沒有量測真實的載入時間、行動版版面或螢幕閱讀器行為。","kicker_zh":"原創分析"}],"roadmap":[{"title":"Phase 1 · Make the current work reproducible","title_zh":"階段一 · 讓現有工作可重現","when":"0–3 months","when_zh":"0–3 個月","lede":"Before building anything new, make what already exists survivable by the next cohort.","lede_zh":"在建造新東西之前，先讓既有成果能被下一屆接手。","items":["**Put every analysis in version control.** One GEMS Research GitHub organisation, one repository per project, with the raw data, the notebook and the figure-generating script in the same place. If a figure cannot be regenerated from the repository, it does not count as a result.","**Write down the measurement protocols.** Calibration standards, units, replicate counts, how uncertainty was computed. The 2026 Best Measurement teams all did this; it is the cheapest credibility a dry lab can buy.","**Standardise the environment.** One `environment.yml` or `requirements.txt` per project, Python 3.12+, pinned versions. A student should be able to clone and run in under ten minutes.","**Archive the 2026 ReLEAF dry lab properly** — the OD600 signal processing, the optogenetic circuit model, the hardware firmware — as the first entry in the institutional record.","**Write the one-page biosecurity and ordering policy.** The US National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening (November 2026) now ties federal funding to buying synthetic DNA only from certified providers that screen orders of 50+ nucleotides. Mirror it: certified suppliers only, a documented internal review of any sequence design, an explicit scope statement excluding pathogen and toxin sequences, signed by every student before their first order. It costs an afternoon and it is the first thing a serious partner asks about."],"items_zh":["**把所有分析放進版本控制。** 一個 GEMS Research GitHub organisation，一個專案一個 repository，原始資料、notebook 與產生圖表的腳本放在同一處。若一張圖無法從 repository 重新產生，它就不算結果。","**寫下量測流程。** 校正標準品、單位、重複次數、不確定度如何計算。2026 年所有最佳量測獎團隊都做到了這點；這是乾實驗室能買到最便宜的可信度。","**統一環境。** 每個專案一份 `environment.yml` 或 `requirements.txt`，Python 3.12 以上，版本鎖定。學生應該能在十分鐘內 clone 下來就跑起來。","**妥善歸檔 2026 ReLEAF 的乾實驗室成果** —— OD600 訊號處理、光遺傳電路模型、硬體韌體 —— 作為機構紀錄的第一筆。","**寫下一頁的生物安全與訂購政策。** 美國《核酸合成篩查國家政策》（2026 年 11 月）已將聯邦經費與「只向通過認證、且會篩查 50 個核苷酸以上訂單的供應商購買合成 DNA」綁在一起。比照辦理：僅限認證供應商、任何序列設計都要有書面內部審查、明確排除病原與毒素序列，並由每位學生在第一次下單前簽署。這只需要一個下午，而且是認真的合作對象第一個會問的事。"],"outcome":"A new student can reproduce any 2026 figure from the repository alone, without asking anybody.","outcome_zh":"新進學生只靠 repository 就能重現 2026 年的任何一張圖，不需要問任何人。"},{"title":"Phase 2 · Build the core modelling skill","title_zh":"階段二 · 建立核心建模能力","when":"3–9 months","when_zh":"3–9 個月","lede":"Two tracks, taught deliberately, with a real deliverable at the end of each.","lede_zh":"兩條軌道，刻意教學，每條都有真實的產出。","items":["**Track A — dynamical systems.** ODE models of genetic circuits, parameter fitting to the team's own data, sensitivity analysis, identifiability. Tools: Python with SciPy and lmfit, Tellurium/COPASI for the SBML side. Deliverable: a circuit model fitted to real GEMS time-course data, with confidence intervals on every parameter.","**Track B — structural and sequence modelling.** Structure prediction is now free infrastructure: the open models (Boltz-2, Chai-1, OpenFold3, ColabFold) match or beat the gated flagship, so folding a protein is a commodity step, not a project. Put one shared GPU box or a modest cloud budget behind an internal queue, make \"fold it, then read the confidence metrics\" compulsory in every project, and teach the hard part — knowing when pLDDT and PAE are lying to you. Deliverable: a designed or selected variant with a documented computational rationale, taken to the bench.","**Teach uncertainty before teaching models.** Error propagation, replicate design, what a fit actually claims. Most student models fail here, not at the mathematics.","**Run a weekly dry-lab clinic.** One hour, somebody presents a figure, everyone else attacks it. This is how modelling taste transmits between cohorts."],"items_zh":["**軌道 A —— 動力系統。** 基因電路的 ODE 模型、以自身資料擬合參數、敏感度分析、可辨識性。工具：Python 搭配 SciPy 與 lmfit，SBML 端使用 Tellurium/COPASI。產出：一個以 GEMS 真實時間序列資料擬合的電路模型，每個參數都附信賴區間。","**軌道 B —— 結構與序列建模。** 結構預測現在已是免費的基礎設施：開源模型（Boltz-2、Chai-1、OpenFold3、ColabFold）已可匹敵甚至超越封閉的旗艦模型，因此「把蛋白質折出來」是一個標準步驟，而不是一個專案。配置一台共用 GPU 主機或一筆適度的雲端預算，架一個內部排程佇列，規定每個專案都必須「先折、再讀信心指標」，並教真正困難的部分——判斷 pLDDT 與 PAE 什麼時候在騙你。產出：一個經過設計或篩選的變體，附上完整的運算理由，並實際進到實驗檯。","**先教不確定度，再教模型。** 誤差傳遞、重複設計、一次擬合究竟主張了什麼。多數學生模型敗在這裡，而不是數學。","**每週一次乾實驗室診療會。** 一小時，一個人報一張圖，其他人負責挑戰它。建模的品味就是這樣在屆與屆之間傳下去的。"],"outcome":"Two or three students who can independently build, fit and defend a model — and who can teach the next two or three.","outcome_zh":"有兩三位學生能獨立建立、擬合並為自己的模型辯護——並且能教會下兩三位。"},{"title":"Phase 3 · Ship one tool the outside world uses","title_zh":"階段三 · 做出一個外界真的會用的工具","when":"9–18 months","when_zh":"9–18 個月","lede":"The difference between a competition team and a research centre is whether anybody outside uses what you built.","lede_zh":"競賽團隊與研究中心的差別，在於外界有沒有人用你做的東西。","items":["**Commit to the Bacillus optogenetics line.** Both trend reviews independently pointed here. Port and properly characterise a CcaS/CcaR or LOV-based light-inducible cassette in *B. subtilis* with full dose-response, dynamic range and growth-stage characterisation. In a twelve-paper literature that is on its own a publishable contribution, and it is the natural continuation of ReLEAF rather than a fresh start.","**Pick one narrow, real problem** that GEMS has genuine data on — the strongest candidate is the optogenetic induction and OD600 measurement work from ReLEAF, where GEMS already has instrumentation, data and a Best Measurement award behind it.","**Buy the domain and host it before the freeze.** This is the single habit that separated the award-winning iGEM 2026 software that is still usable today from the software that is not. Of 21 award-winning tools checked, 8 are live; every one of those was hosted on freeze day, and every source-only tool's wiki lists localhost as its only address. It is a hosting decision made months early, not a coding or budget one — two high-school teams out-shipped most of the universities on exactly this. Write the documentation around a URL, not an install command.","**Build it as a deployed web tool, not a notebook.** Documented, licensed, with example data, a DOI, and a URL anybody can open. Teams that only publish source code get used by nobody.","**Design for other people's data from day one.** Input format, validation, error messages. This is the single most common failure in iGEM software.","**Expect nobody to come.** Across every award-winning 2026 repository checked, stars and forks were zero, and the only external-adoption figure found anywhere was Stanford's SynBase reporting 837 learners. Uni-Padua-IT publicly offered to optimise any team's sequence and got no replies, and said so on their wiki. Publishing is necessary and not sufficient: the three outside users below have to be recruited by hand.","**Get three outside users and write down what broke.** Other Taiwanese schools, a university lab, a 2027 iGEM team. Their complaints are the roadmap for version two."],"items_zh":["**確立枯草桿菌光遺傳學這條路線。** 兩份趨勢分析各自獨立地指向這裡。在 *B. subtilis* 中移植並完整表徵一組 CcaS/CcaR 或 LOV 型的光誘導卡匣，做出完整的劑量反應、動態範圍與生長期表徵。在一個只有十二篇文獻的領域裡，光是這件事本身就足以發表，而且這是 ReLEAF 的自然延伸，不是重新開始。","**挑一個狹窄而真實的問題**，而且 GEMS 手上有真正的資料——最強的候選是 ReLEAF 的光遺傳誘導與 OD600 量測工作，GEMS 已經有儀器、有資料，背後還有一座最佳量測獎。","**在 wiki 凍結前就把網域買好、把服務架起來。** 這是唯一一個把「今天還能用」的 iGEM 2026 得獎軟體，和「今天不能用」的區分開來的習慣。在檢查的 21 個得獎工具中，有 8 個仍然在線；這 8 個無一例外在凍結當日就已經上線，而所有只有原始碼的工具，其 wiki 上唯一的位址都是 localhost。這是一個提前好幾個月做的「要不要架站」決定，不是寫程式或預算的決定——有兩支高中隊伍正是靠這一點，交付得比多數大學還好。文件要圍繞一個網址來寫，而不是圍繞一行安裝指令。","**把它做成已部署的網頁工具，而不是 notebook。** 有文件、有授權、有範例資料、有 DOI，以及任何人都能打開的網址。只釋出原始碼的團隊，沒有人會用。","**從第一天就為別人的資料設計。** 輸入格式、驗證、錯誤訊息。這是 iGEM 軟體最常見的單一失敗原因。","**不要期待有人會自己找上門。** 在檢查過的每一個 2026 得獎 repository 中，star 與 fork 都是零，而唯一能找到的外部採用數字，是 Stanford 的 SynBase 回報的 837 位學習者。Uni-Padua-IT 公開表示願意為任何團隊最佳化序列，結果沒有人回應，而他們把這件事寫在 wiki 上。釋出是必要條件而非充分條件：下面那三位外部使用者，必須一個一個親手去找。","**找到三位外部使用者，並記錄哪裡壞了。** 其他台灣學校、一間大學實驗室、一支 2027 iGEM 團隊。他們的抱怨就是第二版的路線圖。"],"outcome":"A tool with a URL, a licence, documentation and users who are not GEMS students.","outcome_zh":"一個有網址、有授權、有文件，而且使用者不是 GEMS 學生的工具。"},{"title":"Phase 4 · Become a place other people come to","title_zh":"階段四 · 成為別人會來的地方","when":"18 months +","when_zh":"18 個月以上","lede":"Institutional standing comes from being useful to people who owe you nothing.","lede_zh":"機構地位來自於：對那些不欠你任何東西的人仍然有用。","items":["**Run a dry-lab school for Taiwanese iGEM and high-school teams.** Modelling, measurement, reproducibility. Teaching forces the material to become transmissible, and it builds the network that later supplies collaborators.","**Publish.** A methods paper, a preprint, or a well-documented dataset. One citable artefact per year changes how every later conversation starts.","**Keep a standing partnership with a university lab and a non-academic stakeholder** — a farm, a clinic, a municipal body. The stakeholder relationship is what makes human practices real rather than performed, and it is the thing competition teams cannot build in nine months.","**Maintain the trend watch.** This report should be regenerated at least twice a year; the academic and industry tabs are built to be re-run."],"items_zh":["**為台灣的 iGEM 與高中團隊辦一所乾實驗室學校。** 建模、量測、可重現性。教學會逼迫內容變得可傳遞，也建立起日後提供合作者的人脈網絡。","**發表。** 一篇方法論文、一份預印本，或一套文件完整的資料集。每年一個可被引用的產物，會改變此後每一次對話的起點。","**與一間大學實驗室和一個非學術利害關係人維持長期夥伴關係** —— 一座農場、一間診所、一個地方機關。利害關係人關係是讓人類實踐成為真實而非表演的關鍵，也是競賽團隊在九個月內建立不起來的東西。","**持續追蹤趨勢。** 這份報告每年至少重新生成兩次；學術與產業頁就是為了可重跑而設計的。"],"outcome":"GEMS Research is cited, invited and asked for help by people who were never GEMS students.","outcome_zh":"GEMS Research 被從未是 GEMS 學生的人引用、邀請並尋求協助。"}]};
